{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ErYhCY2XXKM5RddJjRcb19","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t<!doctype html>\n2\t<html lang=\"en\">\n3\t<head>\n4\t<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n5\t<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n6\t<title>AI Hub Session Harness</title>\n7\t<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Test a game against the AI Hub Session Protocol: 1–4 copies next to each other on a simulated network.\">\n8\t<style>\n9\t  :root { color-scheme: dark; --bg: #0e0c14; --panel: #191623; --line: #2c2838; --ink: #ece8f4; --dim: #9a93ab; --ok: #4ade80; --bad: #f87171; --warn: #fbbf24; }\n10\t  * { box-sizing: border-box; }\n11\t  html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: var(--bg); color: var(--ink); font: 14px/1.4 system-ui, sans-serif; }\n12\t  body { display: grid; grid-template-rows: auto 1fr; }\n13\t  header { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px 14px; align-items: center; padding: 8px 12px; background: var(--panel); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }\n14\t  header h1 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 8px 0 0; }\n15\t  header label { color: var(--dim); display: inline-flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center; }\n16\t  input, select, button { font: inherit; color: var(--ink); background: #241f31; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 6px; padding: 4px 8px; }\n17\t  input[type=number] { width: 70px; }\n18\t  input.game { width: 300px; }\n19\t  button { cursor: pointer; }\n20\t  button:hover { border-color: var(--dim); }\n21\t  main { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 340px; min-height: 0; }\n22\t  #grid { display: grid; gap: 6px; padding: 6px; min-height: 0; }\n23\t  .cell { position: relative; display: grid; grid-template-rows: auto 1fr; min-height: 0; border: 2px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; background: #000; }\n24\t  .cell__bar { display: flex; gap: 8px; align-items: center; padding: 3px 8px; background: var(--panel); font-size: 12px; }\n25\t  .cell__dot { width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 50%; }\n26\t  .cell__state { margin-left: auto; color: var(--dim); }\n27\t  .cell iframe { width: 100%; height: 100%; border: 0; background: #000; }\n28\t  .cell.is-out { opacity: .35; }\n29\t  aside { display: grid; grid-template-rows: auto auto 1fr; min-height: 0; border-left: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--panel); }\n30\t  aside section { padding: 8px 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }\n31\t  aside h2 { font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .06em; color: var(--dim); margin: 0 0 6px; }\n32\t  #checks li { list-style: none; }\n33\t  #checks ul { margin: 0; padding: 0; }\n34\t  .ok::before { content: '✓ '; color: var(--ok); }\n35\t  .bad::before { content: '✗ '; color: var(--bad); }\n36\t  .wait::before { content: '… '; color: var(--warn); }\n37\t  #log { overflow: auto; font: 12px/1.35 ui-monospace, monospace; padding: 8px 12px; margin: 0; white-space: pre-wrap; }\n38\t  #round { white-space: pre-wrap; font-size: 13px; }\n39\t  .hint { color: var(--dim); }\n40\t</style>\n41\t</head>\n42\t<body>\n43\t<header>\n44\t  <h1>AI Hub session harness</h1>\n45\t  <label>Game <input class=\"game\" id=\"game\" placeholder=\"mygame.html or /games/mygame/index.html\"></label>\n46\t  <label>Players <select id=\"players\"><option>1</option><option selected>2</option><option>3</option><option>4</option></select></label>\n47\t  <label>Latency <input type=\"number\" id=\"latency\" min=\"0\" value=\"60\"> ms</label>\n48\t  <label>Jitter <input type=\"number\" id=\"jitter\" min=\"0\" value=\"20\"> ms</label>\n49\t  <label>Loss <input type=\"number\" id=\"loss\" min=\"0\" max=\"50\" value=\"0\"> %</label>\n50\t  <button id=\"restart\" type=\"button\">New round</button>\n51\t  <button id=\"release\" type=\"button\" title=\"End the splash now: the round starts once every game has loaded\">Start now</button>\n52\t  <button id=\"timeup\" type=\"button\">Time up</button>\n53\t  <label>Remove <select id=\"who\"></select></label>\n54\t  <button id=\"remove\" type=\"button\">Remove player</button>\n55\t  <button id=\"hide\" type=\"button\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Hide host tab</button>\n56\t</header>\n57\t<main>\n58\t  <div id=\"grid\"><p class=\"hint\" style=\"padding:16px\">Name a game above (a path or URL served alongside this page), then press New round. Click a player's frame to control that player.</p></div>\n59\t  <aside>\n60\t    <section><h2>Round</h2><div id=\"round\" class=\"hint\">No round yet.</div></section>\n61\t    <section id=\"checks\"><h2>Conformance</h2><ul id=\"checklist\"><li class=\"hint\">Run with <code>?auto=1</code> for the automatic checks.</li></ul></section>\n62\t    <pre id=\"log\" aria-live=\"off\"></pre>\n63\t  </aside>\n64\t</main>\n65\t<script type=\"module\">\n66\timport { createBridge, attachFrame, postTo, createLocalNetwork } from './bridge.js';\n67\timport { createRound, limitFor, modeOf, seedsRandom, SELF_REPORTED, TIMINGS } from './round.js';\n68\t\n69\tconst NAMES = ['Red Fox', 'Blue Otter', 'Green Heron', 'Gold Lynx'];\n70\tconst params = new URLSearchParams(location.search);\n71\tconst $ = (id) => document.getElementById(id);\n72\tconst auto = params.get('auto') === '1';\n73\tconst scenario = params.get('scenario') || 'standard';\n74\t/** ?scenario=server: the shared world runs on one more copy with no player of its own, as a dedicated server would run it. */\n75\tconst serverMode = scenario === 'server';\n76\tconst playMs = Number(params.get('play')) || 6000;\n77\tconst SPLASH_MS = 10_000;\n78\t\n79\tfor (const [id, key] of [['game', 'game'], ['players', 'players'], ['latency', 'latency'], ['jitter', 'jitter'], ['loss', 'loss']]) {\n80\t  if (params.has(key)) $(id).value = params.get(key);\n81\t}\n82\t\n83\tconst net = createLocalNetwork({});\n84\tlet current = null;\n85\tlet roundNo = 0;\n86\tconst logLines = [];\n87\tfunction log(text) {\n88\t  const t = (performance.now() / 1000).toFixed(2).padStart(7);\n89\t  logLines.push(`${t}  ${text}`);\n90\t  if (logLines.length > 400) logLines.splice(0, logLines.length - 400);\n91\t  $('log').textContent = logLines.join('\\n');\n92\t  $('log').scrollTop = $('log').scrollHeight;\n93\t}\n94\t\n95\t/** The game's head metas, when the page can be fetched from here. */\n96\tasync function metasOf(url) {\n97\t  try {\n98\t    const html = await (await fetch(url)).text();\n99\t    const doc = new DOMParser().parseFromString(html, 'text/html');\n100\t    const meta = (name) => doc.querySelector(`meta[name=\"${name}\"]`)?.getAttribute('content')?.trim() ?? null;\n101\t    return {\n102\t      session: meta('hub:session'),\n103\t      players: meta('hub:session-players'),\n104\t      mode: meta('hub:session-mode'),\n105\t      minutes: meta('hub:session-minutes'),\n106\t    };\n107\t  } catch {\n108\t    return null;\n109\t  }\n110\t}\n111\t\n112\t/**\n113\t * For a game tagged parallel or ghost, the seed rides in the address: the client seeds Math.random with it before the game's scripts run.\n114\t * Only a page of this site is loaded: ?game= comes from the address bar, and a javascript: or another site's\n115\t * address in an unsandboxed frame would run as this origin, where a signed-in player's session is kept.\n116\t */\n117\tconst gameUrl = (game, { tag, seed } = {}) => {\n118\t  let url;\n119\t  try {\n120\t    url = new URL(game, location.href);\n121\t  } catch {\n122\t    return null;\n123\t  }\n124\t  if (url.origin !== location.origin || !/^https?:$/.test(url.protocol)) return null;\n125\t  url.searchParams.set('aihub', '1');\n126\t  if (seedsRandom(tag)) url.searchParams.set('aihub-seed', String(seed >>> 0));\n127\t  return url.href;\n128\t};\n129\t\n130\tfunction applyNet() {\n131\t  Object.assign(net.settings, {\n132\t    latency: Math.max(0, Number($('latency').value) || 0),\n133\t    jitter: Math.max(0, Number($('jitter').value) || 0),\n134\t    loss: Math.min(0.5, Math.max(0, (Number($('loss').value) || 0) / 100)),\n135\t  });\n136\t}\n137\t\n138\t/** Wrap what a game must not call in hub mode, where the page can reach it. */\n139\tfunction instrument(cell) {\n140\t  try {\n141\t    const win = cell.frame.contentWindow;\n142\t    for (const name of ['alert', 'confirm', 'prompt', 'open']) {\n143\t      const original = win[name];\n144\t      win[name] = (...args) => {\n145\t        cell.violations.push(`${name}() called`);\n146\t        log(`${cell.name}: ${name}() called — not allowed in a session`);\n147\t        return name === 'confirm' ? false : name === 'prompt' ? null : undefined;\n148\t      };\n149\t      void original;\n150\t    }\n151\t    win.addEventListener('error', (e) => cell.violations.push(`error: ${e.message}`));\n152\t    win.addEventListener('unhandledrejection', (e) => cell.violations.push(`unhandled rejection: ${e.reason?.message || e.reason}`));\n153\t  } catch {\n154\t    cell.instrumented = false;\n155\t  }\n156\t}\n157\t\n158\tasync function newRound() {\n159\t  endCurrent();\n160\t  applyNet();\n161\t  const game = $('game').value.trim();\n162\t  if (!game) return null;\n163\t  if (!gameUrl(game)) {\n164\t    log(`Not loading ${game}: the harness only plays pages from this site.`);\n165\t    return null;\n166\t  }\n167\t  const n = Math.max(1, Math.min(4, Number($('players').value) || 2));\n168\t  const metas = await metasOf(game);\n169\t  const mode = modeOf(metas?.mode);\n170\t  const limitMs = params.has('limit') ? Number(params.get('limit')) * 1000 : limitFor(metas?.minutes);\n171\t  const seed = params.has('seed') ? Number(params.get('seed')) >>> 0 : crypto.getRandomValues(new Uint32Array(1))[0];\n172\t  const round = ++roundNo;\n173\t  const players = Array.from({ length: n }, (_, slot) => ({ key: `p${slot}`, slot, name: NAMES[slot] }));\n174\t  const hubEnd = net.endpoint('hub');\n175\t  const grid = $('grid');\n176\t  grid.replaceChildren();\n177\t  const copies = n + (serverMode ? 1 : 0);\n178\t  grid.style.gridTemplateColumns = copies > 1 ? '1fr 1fr' : '1fr';\n179\t  grid.style.gridTemplateRows = `repeat(${Math.ceil(copies / (copies > 1 ? 2 : 1))}, 1fr)`;\n180\t\n181\t  const state = { round, n, metas, mode, limitMs, seed, players, cells: [], hubEnd, status: null, record: null, hidden: false, splashUntil: performance.now() + SPLASH_MS, answers: { ready: new Set(), more: new Set() } };\n182\t  current = state;\n183\t  log(`round ${round}: ${n} player${n > 1 ? 's' : ''}, seed ${seed}, limit ${Math.round(limitMs / 1000)} s, mode ${mode || '(from hello)'}`);\n184\t\n185\t  state.coordinator = createRound({\n186\t    round,\n187\t    players,\n188\t    hostKey: 'p0',\n189\t    serverKey: serverMode ? 'server' : null,\n190\t    mode,\n191\t    seed,\n192\t    limitMs,\n193\t    gate: true,\n194\t    deliver: (key, m) => hubEnd.send(key, { k: 'h', r: round, m }),\n195\t    onStatus: (s) => { state.status = s; render(state); },\n196\t    onEnd: (record) => {\n197\t      state.record = record;\n198\t      log(`round ${round} ${record.status}: ${record.reason}${record.standings ? ' — standings ' + JSON.stringify(record.standings) : ''}`);\n199\t      render(state);\n200\t    },\n201\t  });\n202\t  hubEnd.onMessage((from, env) => {\n203\t    if (env.k !== 'c' || env.r !== round) return;\n204\t    if (env.m?.type !== 'vis') log(`${from} → hub: ${env.m?.type}${env.m?.type === 'result' ? ' ' + JSON.stringify({ time: env.m.time, score: env.m.score }) : ''}${env.m?.type === 'finish' ? ' ' + JSON.stringify(env.m.standings) : ''}`);\n205\t    state.coordinator.receive(from, env.m);\n206\t  });\n207\t\n208\t  for (const p of [...players, ...(serverMode ? [{ key: 'server', slot: null, name: 'Server', server: true }] : [])]) {\n209\t    const color = p.server ? '#8a8a8a' : ['#e8443a', '#3b82f6', '#22c55e', '#f5b700'][p.slot];\n210\t    const frame = document.createElement('iframe');\n211\t    frame.allow = 'fullscreen; autoplay; gamepad; pointer-lock';\n212\t    frame.title = p.name;\n213\t    const label = document.createElement('div');\n214\t    label.className = 'cell__bar';\n215\t    label.innerHTML = `<span class=\"cell__dot\" style=\"background:${color}\"></span><b></b><span class=\"cell__state\"></span>`;\n216\t    label.querySelector('b').textContent = `${p.name} (${p.key})`;\n217\t    const el = document.createElement('div');\n218\t    el.className = 'cell';\n219\t    el.style.borderColor = color;\n220\t    el.append(label, frame);\n221\t    grid.append(el);\n222\t\n223\t    const endpoint = net.endpoint(p.key);\n224\t    const cell = { ...p, el, label, frame, endpoint, violations: [], instrumented: true, gone: false, progress: [], cardSent: '' };\n225\t    const post = postTo(frame);\n226\t    cell.bridge = createBridge({\n227\t      key: p.key,\n228\t      round,\n229\t      coordinator: 'hub',\n230\t      post: (msg) => {\n231\t        if (msg.type !== 'message') log(`hub → ${p.key}: ${msg.type}${msg.type === 'start' ? ` in ${msg.in} ms` : ''}${msg.type === 'leave' ? ` ${msg.id} (${msg.reason})` : ''}${msg.type === 'end' ? ` ${msg.reason}` : ''}`);\n232\t        post(msg);\n233\t      },\n234\t      net: endpoint,\n235\t      onIssue: (i) => log(`${p.key} ✗ ${i.problem}`),\n236\t      onFullscreen: (on) => log(`${p.key} asked for fullscreen ${on ? 'on' : 'off'}: the hub's page takes it`),\n237\t      onAnswer: (what) => answerCard(state, cell, what),\n238\t      // The scoreboard's feed: this cell's own progress, as its bridge passes it on.\n239\t      onProgress: (id, report) => {\n240\t        if (id !== cell.bridge?.me) return;\n241\t        cell.progress.push({ at: performance.now(), ...report });\n242\t        state.coordinator.progress(id, report.score);\n243\t        render(state);\n244\t      },\n245\t    });\n246\t    endpoint.onMessage((from, env) => cell.bridge.fromNet(from, env));\n247\t    cell.detach = attachFrame(frame, (msg) => cell.bridge.fromGame(msg));\n248\t    frame.addEventListener('load', () => instrument(cell), { once: true });\n249\t    frame.src = gameUrl(game, { tag: metas?.mode, seed });\n250\t    state.cells.push(cell);\n251\t  }\n252\t  renderWho(state);\n253\t  render(state);\n254\t  // By hand, the card lifts by itself after ten seconds (more when a player asks), as in a session;\n255\t  // the conformance run releases it itself.\n256\t  const ticker = setInterval(() => {\n257\t    if (state !== current || state.coordinator.released) return clearInterval(ticker);\n258\t    if (!auto && performance.now() >= state.splashUntil) return releaseRound(state);\n259\t    tickCard(state);\n260\t  }, 250);\n261\t  return state;\n262\t}\n263\t\n264\tfunction releaseRound(state = current) {\n265\t  if (!state || state !== current || state.coordinator.released) return;\n266\t  state.splashUntil = null;\n267\t  tickCard(state);\n268\t  log('splash over: the round starts once every game has loaded');\n269\t  state.coordinator.release();\n270\t}\n271\t\n272\t/** A game's own card, as the hub drives it: the countdown and who is ready, to every copy that shows one. */\n273\tfunction tickCard(state) {\n274\t  const left = state.splashUntil === null ? null : Math.max(0, state.splashUntil - performance.now());\n275\t  const ready = state.cells.filter((c) => state.answers.ready.has(c.key)).map((c) => c.bridge.me);\n276\t  for (const cell of state.cells) {\n277\t    if (cell.gone || !cell.bridge.showsCard) continue;\n278\t    const card = { left, paused: false, starting: left === null, ready, asking: state.answers.more.size, asked: state.answers.more.has(cell.key) };\n279\t    const id = JSON.stringify({ ...card, left: left === null ? null : Math.ceil(left / 1000) });\n280\t    if (cell.cardSent === id) continue;\n281\t    cell.cardSent = id;\n282\t    cell.bridge.card(card);\n283\t  }\n284\t}\n285\t\n286\t/** A player answered on the game's own card: Ready, or more time (+10 s; again takes it back). */\n287\tfunction answerCard(state, cell, what) {\n288\t  if (state !== current || state.coordinator.released || cell.server) return;\n289\t  const { ready, more } = state.answers;\n290\t  if (what === 'ready') {\n291\t    ready.add(cell.key);\n292\t    more.delete(cell.key);\n293\t  } else if (more.has(cell.key)) {\n294\t    more.delete(cell.key);\n295\t  } else {\n296\t    more.add(cell.key);\n297\t    ready.delete(cell.key);\n298\t    state.splashUntil += 10_000;\n299\t  }\n300\t  log(`${cell.key} answers ${what} on the game's card`);\n301\t  const players = state.cells.filter((c) => !c.server && !c.gone);\n302\t  if (!auto && players.every((c) => ready.has(c.key))) return releaseRound(state);\n303\t  tickCard(state);\n304\t}\n305\t\n306\tfunction endCurrent() {\n307\t  if (!current) return;\n308\t  current.coordinator.abort('session-ended');\n309\t  for (const cell of current.cells) removeCell(cell, false);\n310\t  current.hubEnd.close();\n311\t  current = null;\n312\t}\n313\t\n314\tfunction removeCell(cell, tellRound = true) {\n315\t  if (cell.gone) return;\n316\t  cell.gone = true;\n317\t  cell.detach();\n318\t  cell.endpoint.close();\n319\t  cell.frame.remove();\n320\t  cell.el.classList.add('is-out');\n321\t  if (tellRound) {\n322\t    log(`${cell.key} left`);\n323\t    current?.coordinator.leave(cell.key, 'left');\n324\t  }\n325\t}\n326\t\n327\tfunction renderWho(state) {\n328\t  $('who').replaceChildren(...state.cells.map((c) => new Option(`${c.name} (${c.key})${c.server ? ' — host, no player' : c.slot === 0 && !serverMode ? ' — host' : ''}`, c.key)));\n329\t}\n330\t\n331\tfunction render(state) {\n332\t  const s = state.status;\n333\t  if (!s) return;\n334\t  for (const cell of state.cells) {\n335\t    const p = s.players.find((q) => q.key === cell.key) ?? (s.server?.key === cell.key ? s.server : null);\n336\t    if (!p) continue;\n337\t    const bits = [];\n338\t    if (p.out) bits.push(`out: ${p.out}`);\n339\t    else if (p.result) bits.push(`result ${JSON.stringify(p.result)}`);\n340\t    else if (p.ready) bits.push('ready');\n341\t    else if (p.hello) bits.push('welcomed');\n342\t    else bits.push('loading');\n343\t    const last = cell.progress.at(-1);\n344\t    if (last && !p.result) bits.push(`progress ${last.score}${last.label ? ` (${last.label})` : ''}`);\n345\t    bits.push(`↑${cell.bridge.stats.sent} ↓${cell.bridge.stats.received}`);\n346\t    cell.label.querySelector('.cell__state').textContent = bits.join(' · ');\n347\t    cell.el.classList.toggle('is-out', !!p.out || cell.gone);\n348\t  }\n349\t  const lines = [`Round ${s.round} · ${s.mode || 'mode unknown'} · phase ${s.phase}`, `Host: ${s.server ? 'the server, no player' : `player ${s.host}`} · seed ${state.seed}`];\n350\t  if (s.gate && !s.released) lines.push(`Card: ${state.cells.some((c) => c.bridge.showsCard) ? 'the game’s own, ' : ''}${state.splashUntil ? `${Math.max(0, Math.ceil((state.splashUntil - performance.now()) / 1000))} s left` : 'held'} (Start now ends it)`);\n351\t  if (state.record) {\n352\t    const name = (id) => s.players[id]?.name ?? `#${id}`;\n353\t    lines.push(`Ended ${state.record.status} (${state.record.reason})`);\n354\t    if (state.record.standings) state.record.standings.forEach((ids, i) => lines.push(`  ${i + 1}. ${ids.map(name).join(', ')}`));\n355\t  }\n356\t  if (s.issues.length) lines.push(...s.issues.map((i) => `✗ ${i.key}: ${i.problem}`));\n357\t  $('round').textContent = lines.join('\\n');\n358\t}\n359\t\n360\t$('restart').onclick = () => newRound();\n361\t$('release').onclick = () => releaseRound();\n362\t$('timeup').onclick = () => current?.coordinator.timeUp();\n363\t$('remove').onclick = () => {\n364\t  const cell = current?.cells.find((c) => c.key === $('who').value);\n365\t  if (cell) removeCell(cell);\n366\t};\n367\t$('hide').onclick = () => {\n368\t  if (!current) return;\n369\t  current.hidden = !current.hidden;\n370\t  $('hide').setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(current.hidden));\n371\t  (current.cells.find((c) => c.server) ?? current.cells[0])?.bridge.visibility(current.hidden);\n372\t  log(`host tab ${current.hidden ? 'hidden' : 'shown'}`);\n373\t};\n374\tfor (const id of ['latency', 'jitter', 'loss']) $(id).onchange = applyNet;\n375\t\n376\t/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n377\t * ?auto=1 — the conformance run. It presses keys inside each frame with\n378\t * synthetic events while the round plays (the frames must be served from this\n379\t * page's origin). Results land in window.__hubCheck, and body[data-complete]\n380\t * turns \"true\".\n381\t * ------------------------------------------------------------------------- */\n382\t\n383\tconst sleep = (ms) => new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, ms));\n384\tasync function until(test, ms) {\n385\t  const end = performance.now() + ms;\n386\t  while (performance.now() < end) {\n387\t    if (test()) return true;\n388\t    await sleep(50);\n389\t  }\n390\t  return test();\n391\t}\n392\t\n393\tfunction poke(cell, key) {\n394\t  const doc = cell.frame.contentDocument;\n395\t  const win = cell.frame.contentWindow;\n396\t  if (!doc || !win) return false;\n397\t  const target = doc.activeElement && doc.activeElement !== doc.documentElement ? doc.activeElement : doc.body || doc.documentElement;\n398\t  const init = { key, code: key === ' ' ? 'Space' : key, bubbles: true, cancelable: true, view: win };\n399\t  target.dispatchEvent(new win.KeyboardEvent('keydown', init));\n400\t  setTimeout(() => target.dispatchEvent(new win.KeyboardEvent('keyup', init)), 120);\n401\t  return true;\n402\t}\n403\t\n404\tasync function conformance() {\n405\t  const checks = [];\n406\t  const check = (name, pass, detail = '') => {\n407\t    checks.push({ name, pass: !!pass, detail });\n408\t    renderChecks(checks);\n409\t    return !!pass;\n410\t  };\n411\t  const report = { done: false, pass: false, game: $('game').value, players: Number($('players').value), scenario, checks, log: logLines };\n412\t  window.__hubCheck = report;\n413\t  try {\n414\t    const state = await newRound();\n415\t    if (!state) {\n416\t      check('game named', false, 'pass ?game=<path> of a page on this site');\n417\t      return;\n418\t    }\n419\t    const n = state.n;\n420\t    const m = state.metas;\n421\t    check('head metas', m && m.session === '1' && modeOf(m.mode), m ? `hub:session=${m.session} mode=${m.mode}` : 'could not fetch the page');\n422\t    const seats = String(m?.players ?? '').match(/\\d+/g)?.map(Number) ?? [];\n423\t    const [least, most = least] = seats;\n424\t    check('hub:session-players is a range within 1–4', seats.length >= 1 && seats.length <= 2 && least >= 1 && least <= most && most <= 4, `hub:session-players=${m?.players}`);\n425\t    if (m?.minutes != null) check('hub:session-minutes, when given, is a number', Number(m.minutes) > 0, `hub:session-minutes=${m.minutes}`);\n426\t\n427\t    // Every copy: the players, and in a server round the server's copy.\n428\t    const copies = () => [...(state.status?.players ?? []), ...(state.status?.server ? [state.status.server] : [])];\n429\t    const helloed = await until(() => copies().every((p) => p.hello), TIMINGS.helloMs + 1000);\n430\t    check('every copy says hello', helloed, copies().filter((p) => !p.hello).map((p) => p.key).join(', '));\n431\t    if (!helloed) return;\n432\t    const caps = state.coordinator.seats().map((s) => s.caps);\n433\t    check('hello names protocol 1 and the mode', caps.every((c) => c.v === 1 && modeOf(c.mode) === state.coordinator.mode), JSON.stringify(caps[0]));\n434\t    check('hello seats cover this player count', caps.every((c) => Array.isArray(c.seats) && c.seats[0] <= Math.max(2, n) && c.seats[1] >= n), JSON.stringify(caps[0]?.seats));\n435\t    if (state.cells.some((c) => !c.frame.contentDocument)) {\n436\t      check('frames reachable for synthetic input', false, 'serve the game from the same origin as this harness');\n437\t      return;\n438\t    }\n439\t\n440\t    // The card collects ready: every game readies up by itself once loaded, with no prompt and no key.\n441\t    const loaded = await until(() => copies().every((p) => p.ready), 20_000);\n442\t    check('ready without a key press (the card asks the players)', loaded, copies().filter((p) => !p.ready).map((p) => p.key).join(', '));\n443\t    // A game that shows its own card takes the players' answers on it: Enter is Ready.\n444\t    if (caps.some((c) => c?.card)) {\n445\t      const players = state.cells.filter((c) => !c.server);\n446\t      const sent = await until(() => players.every((c) => c.cardSent), 2000);\n447\t      for (const cell of players) poke(cell, 'Enter');\n448\t      const answered = await until(() => players.every((c) => state.answers.ready.has(c.key)), 3000);\n449\t      check('its own card: Enter answers Ready', sent && answered, players.filter((c) => !state.answers.ready.has(c.key)).map((c) => `${c.key}${c.cardSent ? '' : ' (no card yet)'}`).join(', '));\n450\t    }\n451\t    releaseRound(state);\n452\t    const started = await until(() => state.status?.phase !== 'loading', 15_000);\n453\t    check('the round starts when the card ends', started && copies().every((p) => p.ready), copies().filter((p) => !p.ready).map((p) => p.key).join(', ') || state.status?.phase);\n454\t    if (!started || state.record) return;\n455\t\n456\t    await until(() => state.status.phase === 'playing' || state.record, TIMINGS.countdownMs + 2000);\n457\t    const arrows = ['ArrowLeft', 'ArrowRight', 'ArrowUp', 'ArrowDown', 'a', 'd', 'w', 's'];\n458\t    const randomly = async (ms) => {\n459\t      const end = performance.now() + ms;\n460\t      while (performance.now() < end && !state.record) {\n461\t        for (const cell of state.cells) if (!cell.gone && !cell.server) poke(cell, arrows[Math.floor(Math.random() * arrows.length)]);\n462\t        await sleep(150);\n463\t      }\n464\t    };\n465\t    await randomly(Math.min(1500, playMs / 4));\n466\t\n467\t    const mode = state.coordinator.mode;\n468\t    // Parallel and ghost: every copy runs its own world from the same seeded start. A game\n469\t    // still tagged race was built to race's contract: no seeded start, and no progress asked.\n470\t    const own = SELF_REPORTED.includes(mode);\n471\t    const legacyRace = own && !seedsRandom(m?.mode);\n472\t    if (own && !legacyRace) {\n473\t      const seeded = state.cells.every((c) => c.frame.contentWindow?.AIHub?.seeded === true);\n474\t      check(`${mode}: Math.random is seeded, the same on every copy`, seeded, state.cells.map((c) => `${c.key}: client ${c.frame.contentWindow?.AIHub?.version ?? '?'} seeded ${c.frame.contentWindow?.AIHub?.seeded}`).join('; '));\n475\t    }\n476\t\n477\t    if (scenario === 'host-leave') removeCell(state.cells[0]);\n478\t    else if (n >= 3) removeCell(state.cells[n - 1]);\n479\t    await randomly(playMs / 2);\n480\t    const remaining = state.cells.filter((c) => !c.gone);\n481\t    if (own) {\n482\t      if (mode === 'parallel') {\n483\t        check('parallel: no game traffic', state.cells.every((c) => c.bridge.stats.sent === 0),\n484\t          state.cells.map((c) => `${c.key} ↑${c.bridge.stats.sent}`).join(' '));\n485\t      } else {\n486\t        check('ghost: every copy sends its player', remaining.every((c) => c.bridge.stats.sent > 0) || n === 1,\n487\t          remaining.map((c) => `${c.key} ↑${c.bridge.stats.sent}`).join(' '));\n488\t      }\n489\t      if (!legacyRace) check(`${mode}: every copy reports its progress`, remaining.every((c) => c.progress.length > 0 || state.status?.players.find((p) => p.key === c.key)?.result),\n490\t        remaining.map((c) => `${c.key}: ${c.progress.length} report${c.progress.length === 1 ? '' : 's'}`).join(', '));\n491\t    } else {\n492\t      check('game traffic flows both ways', remaining.every((c) => c.bridge.stats.sent > 0 && c.bridge.stats.received > 0) || n === 1,\n493\t        remaining.map((c) => `${c.key} ↑${c.bridge.stats.sent} ↓${c.bridge.stats.received}`).join(' '));\n494\t    }\n495\t\n496\t    if (!state.record) state.coordinator.timeUp();\n497\t    const ended = await until(() => state.record, TIMINGS.graceMs + 2000);\n498\t    const record = state.record;\n499\t    if (serverMode) {\n500\t      // The world ran on the server: the players heard it, and only the host may finish a shared world.\n501\t      const serverCell = state.cells.find((c) => c.server);\n502\t      check('a copy with no player of its own runs the world (as a server would)', ended && record.status === 'played' && record.hostId === serverCell.bridge.me && serverCell.bridge.stats.sent > 0,\n503\t        record ? `${record.status} (${record.reason}), host ${record.hostId}, server sent ${serverCell.bridge.stats.sent}` : 'no end');\n504\t    }\n505\t    if (scenario === 'host-leave' && !SELF_REPORTED.includes(state.coordinator.mode)) {\n506\t      check('host leaving voids the round', ended && record.status === 'void' && record.endReason === 'host-left', record ? `${record.status} (${record.reason})` : 'no end');\n507\t    } else {\n508\t      check('the round ends with a valid result', ended && record.status === 'played', record ? `${record.status} (${record.reason})` : 'no end within the grace period');\n509\t    }\n510\t    await sleep(300);\n511\t    check('every remaining copy is told the round ended', remaining.every((c) => c.bridge.ended), remaining.filter((c) => !c.bridge.ended).map((c) => c.key).join(', '));\n512\t    const issues = [...(state.status?.issues ?? []), ...state.cells.flatMap((c) => c.bridge.issues)];\n513\t    check('no protocol problems', issues.length === 0, issues.map((i) => `${i.key}: ${i.problem}`).join('; '));\n514\t    const violations = state.cells.flatMap((c) => {\n515\t      let extra = [];\n516\t      try {\n517\t        extra = c.frame.contentWindow?.__hubViolations ?? [];\n518\t      } catch {}\n519\t      return [...c.violations, ...extra].map((v) => `${c.key}: ${v}`);\n520\t    });\n521\t    check('no errors, dialogs, popups or sockets', violations.length === 0, violations.slice(0, 6).join('; '));\n522\t  } catch (error) {\n523\t    check('harness ran', false, String(error?.stack || error));\n524\t  } finally {\n525\t    report.pass = checks.length > 0 && checks.every((c) => c.pass);\n526\t    report.done = true;\n527\t    document.body.dataset.complete = 'true';\n528\t    log(`conformance: ${report.pass ? 'PASS' : 'FAIL'}`);\n529\t  }\n530\t}\n531\t\n532\tfunction renderChecks(checks) {\n533\t  $('checklist').replaceChildren(\n534\t    ...checks.map((c) => {\n535\t      const li = document.createElement('li');\n536\t      li.className = c.pass ? 'ok' : 'bad';\n537\t      li.textContent = c.name + (c.detail && !c.pass ? ` — ${c.detail}` : '');\n538\t      li.title = c.detail;\n539\t      return li;\n540\t    }),\n541\t  );\n542\t}\n543\t\n544\tif (auto) conformance();\n545\telse if ($('game').value) newRound();\n546\t</script>\n547\t</body>\n548\t</html>\n549\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4a882869-9e92-4155-a3b0-121d8fdc660c","uuid":"4e6dde23-958c-4dd4-98f9-8597520df60f","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:20:56.784Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211959__x9a5b1d/work/_research/hub/harness.html","content":"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>AI Hub Session Harness</title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Test a game against the AI Hub Session Protocol: 1–4 copies next to each other on a simulated network.\">\n<style>\n  :root { color-scheme: dark; --bg: #0e0c14; --panel: #191623; --line: #2c2838; --ink: #ece8f4; --dim: #9a93ab; --ok: #4ade80; --bad: #f87171; --warn: #fbbf24; }\n  * { box-sizing: border-box; }\n  html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: var(--bg); color: var(--ink); font: 14px/1.4 system-ui, sans-serif; }\n  body { display: grid; grid-template-rows: auto 1fr; }\n  header { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px 14px; align-items: center; padding: 8px 12px; background: var(--panel); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }\n  header h1 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 8px 0 0; }\n  header label { color: var(--dim); display: inline-flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center; }\n  input, select, button { font: inherit; color: var(--ink); background: #241f31; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 6px; padding: 4px 8px; }\n  input[type=number] { width: 70px; }\n  input.game { width: 300px; }\n  button { cursor: pointer; }\n  button:hover { border-color: var(--dim); }\n  main { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 340px; min-height: 0; }\n  #grid { display: grid; gap: 6px; padding: 6px; min-height: 0; }\n  .cell { position: relative; display: grid; grid-template-rows: auto 1fr; min-height: 0; border: 2px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; background: #000; }\n  .cell__bar { display: flex; gap: 8px; align-items: center; padding: 3px 8px; background: var(--panel); font-size: 12px; }\n  .cell__dot { width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 50%; }\n  .cell__state { margin-left: auto; color: var(--dim); }\n  .cell iframe { width: 100%; height: 100%; border: 0; background: #000; }\n  .cell.is-out { opacity: .35; }\n  aside { display: grid; grid-template-rows: auto auto 1fr; min-height: 0; border-left: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--panel); }\n  aside section { padding: 8px 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }\n  aside h2 { font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .06em; color: var(--dim); margin: 0 0 6px; }\n  #checks li { list-style: none; }\n  #checks ul { margin: 0; padding: 0; }\n  .ok::before { content: '✓ '; color: var(--ok); }\n  .bad::before { content: '✗ '; color: var(--bad); }\n  .wait::before { content: '… '; color: var(--warn); }\n  #log { overflow: auto; font: 12px/1.35 ui-monospace, monospace; padding: 8px 12px; margin: 0; white-space: pre-wrap; }\n  #round { white-space: pre-wrap; font-size: 13px; }\n  .hint { color: var(--dim); }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<header>\n  <h1>AI Hub session harness</h1>\n  <label>Game <input class=\"game\" id=\"game\" placeholder=\"mygame.html or /games/mygame/index.html\"></label>\n  <label>Players <select id=\"players\"><option>1</option><option selected>2</option><option>3</option><option>4</option></select></label>\n  <label>Latency <input type=\"number\" id=\"latency\" min=\"0\" value=\"60\"> ms</label>\n  <label>Jitter <input type=\"number\" id=\"jitter\" min=\"0\" value=\"20\"> ms</label>\n  <label>Loss <input type=\"number\" id=\"loss\" min=\"0\" max=\"50\" value=\"0\"> %</label>\n  <button id=\"restart\" type=\"button\">New round</button>\n  <button id=\"release\" type=\"button\" title=\"End the splash now: the round starts once every game has loaded\">Start now</button>\n  <button id=\"timeup\" type=\"button\">Time up</button>\n  <label>Remove <select id=\"who\"></select></label>\n  <button id=\"remove\" type=\"button\">Remove player</button>\n  <button id=\"hide\" type=\"button\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Hide host tab</button>\n</header>\n<main>\n  <div id=\"grid\"><p class=\"hint\" style=\"padding:16px\">Name a game above (a path or URL served alongside this page), then press New round. Click a player's frame to control that player.</p></div>\n  <aside>\n    <section><h2>Round</h2><div id=\"round\" class=\"hint\">No round yet.</div></section>\n    <section id=\"checks\"><h2>Conformance</h2><ul id=\"checklist\"><li class=\"hint\">Run with <code>?auto=1</code> for the automatic checks.</li></ul></section>\n    <pre id=\"log\" aria-live=\"off\"></pre>\n  </aside>\n</main>\n<script type=\"module\">\nimport { createBridge, attachFrame, postTo, createLocalNetwork } from './bridge.js';\nimport { createRound, limitFor, modeOf, seedsRandom, SELF_REPORTED, TIMINGS } from './round.js';\n\nconst NAMES = ['Red Fox', 'Blue Otter', 'Green Heron', 'Gold Lynx'];\nconst params = new URLSearchParams(location.search);\nconst $ = (id) => document.getElementById(id);\nconst auto = params.get('auto') === '1';\nconst scenario = params.get('scenario') || 'standard';\n/** ?scenario=server: the shared world runs on one more copy with no player of its own, as a dedicated server would run it. */\nconst serverMode = scenario === 'server';\nconst playMs = Number(params.get('play')) || 6000;\nconst SPLASH_MS = 10_000;\n\nfor (const [id, key] of [['game', 'game'], ['players', 'players'], ['latency', 'latency'], ['jitter', 'jitter'], ['loss', 'loss']]) {\n  if (params.has(key)) $(id).value = params.get(key);\n}\n\nconst net = createLocalNetwork({});\nlet current = null;\nlet roundNo = 0;\nconst logLines = [];\nfunction log(text) {\n  const t = (performance.now() / 1000).toFixed(2).padStart(7);\n  logLines.push(`${t}  ${text}`);\n  if (logLines.length > 400) logLines.splice(0, logLines.length - 400);\n  $('log').textContent = logLines.join('\\n');\n  $('log').scrollTop = $('log').scrollHeight;\n}\n\n/** The game's head metas, when the page can be fetched from here. */\nasync function metasOf(url) {\n  try {\n    const html = await (await fetch(url)).text();\n    const doc = new DOMParser().parseFromString(html, 'text/html');\n    const meta = (name) => doc.querySelector(`meta[name=\"${name}\"]`)?.getAttribute('content')?.trim() ?? null;\n    return {\n      session: meta('hub:session'),\n      players: meta('hub:session-players'),\n      mode: meta('hub:session-mode'),\n      minutes: meta('hub:session-minutes'),\n    };\n  } catch {\n    return null;\n  }\n}\n\n/**\n * For a game tagged parallel or ghost, the seed rides in the address: the client seeds Math.random with it before the game's scripts run.\n * Only a page of this site is loaded: ?game= comes from the address bar, and a javascript: or another site's\n * address in an unsandboxed frame would run as this origin, where a signed-in player's session is kept.\n */\nconst gameUrl = (game, { tag, seed } = {}) => {\n  let url;\n  try {\n    url = new URL(game, location.href);\n  } catch {\n    return null;\n  }\n  if (url.origin !== location.origin || !/^https?:$/.test(url.protocol)) return null;\n  url.searchParams.set('aihub', '1');\n  if (seedsRandom(tag)) url.searchParams.set('aihub-seed', String(seed >>> 0));\n  return url.href;\n};\n\nfunction applyNet() {\n  Object.assign(net.settings, {\n    latency: Math.max(0, Number($('latency').value) || 0),\n    jitter: Math.max(0, Number($('jitter').value) || 0),\n    loss: Math.min(0.5, Math.max(0, (Number($('loss').value) || 0) / 100)),\n  });\n}\n\n/** Wrap what a game must not call in hub mode, where the page can reach it. */\nfunction instrument(cell) {\n  try {\n    const win = cell.frame.contentWindow;\n    for (const name of ['alert', 'confirm', 'prompt', 'open']) {\n      const original = win[name];\n      win[name] = (...args) => {\n        cell.violations.push(`${name}() called`);\n        log(`${cell.name}: ${name}() called — not allowed in a session`);\n        return name === 'confirm' ? false : name === 'prompt' ? null : undefined;\n      };\n      void original;\n    }\n    win.addEventListener('error', (e) => cell.violations.push(`error: ${e.message}`));\n    win.addEventListener('unhandledrejection', (e) => cell.violations.push(`unhandled rejection: ${e.reason?.message || e.reason}`));\n  } catch {\n    cell.instrumented = false;\n  }\n}\n\nasync function newRound() {\n  endCurrent();\n  applyNet();\n  const game = $('game').value.trim();\n  if (!game) return null;\n  if (!gameUrl(game)) {\n    log(`Not loading ${game}: the harness only plays pages from this site.`);\n    return null;\n  }\n  const n = Math.max(1, Math.min(4, Number($('players').value) || 2));\n  const metas = await metasOf(game);\n  const mode = modeOf(metas?.mode);\n  const limitMs = params.has('limit') ? Number(params.get('limit')) * 1000 : limitFor(metas?.minutes);\n  const seed = params.has('seed') ? Number(params.get('seed')) >>> 0 : crypto.getRandomValues(new Uint32Array(1))[0];\n  const round = ++roundNo;\n  const players = Array.from({ length: n }, (_, slot) => ({ key: `p${slot}`, slot, name: NAMES[slot] }));\n  const hubEnd = net.endpoint('hub');\n  const grid = $('grid');\n  grid.replaceChildren();\n  const copies = n + (serverMode ? 1 : 0);\n  grid.style.gridTemplateColumns = copies > 1 ? '1fr 1fr' : '1fr';\n  grid.style.gridTemplateRows = `repeat(${Math.ceil(copies / (copies > 1 ? 2 : 1))}, 1fr)`;\n\n  const state = { round, n, metas, mode, limitMs, seed, players, cells: [], hubEnd, status: null, record: null, hidden: false, splashUntil: performance.now() + SPLASH_MS, answers: { ready: new Set(), more: new Set() } };\n  current = state;\n  log(`round ${round}: ${n} player${n > 1 ? 's' : ''}, seed ${seed}, limit ${Math.round(limitMs / 1000)} s, mode ${mode || '(from hello)'}`);\n\n  state.coordinator = createRound({\n    round,\n    players,\n    hostKey: 'p0',\n    serverKey: serverMode ? 'server' : null,\n    mode,\n    seed,\n    limitMs,\n    gate: true,\n    deliver: (key, m) => hubEnd.send(key, { k: 'h', r: round, m }),\n    onStatus: (s) => { state.status = s; render(state); },\n    onEnd: (record) => {\n      state.record = record;\n      log(`round ${round} ${record.status}: ${record.reason}${record.standings ? ' — standings ' + JSON.stringify(record.standings) : ''}`);\n      render(state);\n    },\n  });\n  hubEnd.onMessage((from, env) => {\n    if (env.k !== 'c' || env.r !== round) return;\n    if (env.m?.type !== 'vis') log(`${from} → hub: ${env.m?.type}${env.m?.type === 'result' ? ' ' + JSON.stringify({ time: env.m.time, score: env.m.score }) : ''}${env.m?.type === 'finish' ? ' ' + JSON.stringify(env.m.standings) : ''}`);\n    state.coordinator.receive(from, env.m);\n  });\n\n  for (const p of [...players, ...(serverMode ? [{ key: 'server', slot: null, name: 'Server', server: true }] : [])]) {\n    const color = p.server ? '#8a8a8a' : ['#e8443a', '#3b82f6', '#22c55e', '#f5b700'][p.slot];\n    const frame = document.createElement('iframe');\n    frame.allow = 'fullscreen; autoplay; gamepad; pointer-lock';\n    frame.title = p.name;\n    const label = document.createElement('div');\n    label.className = 'cell__bar';\n    label.innerHTML = `<span class=\"cell__dot\" style=\"background:${color}\"></span><b></b><span class=\"cell__state\"></span>`;\n    label.querySelector('b').textContent = `${p.name} (${p.key})`;\n    const el = document.createElement('div');\n    el.className = 'cell';\n    el.style.borderColor = color;\n    el.append(label, frame);\n    grid.append(el);\n\n    const endpoint = net.endpoint(p.key);\n    const cell = { ...p, el, label, frame, endpoint, violations: [], instrumented: true, gone: false, progress: [], cardSent: '' };\n    const post = postTo(frame);\n    cell.bridge = createBridge({\n      key: p.key,\n      round,\n      coordinator: 'hub',\n      post: (msg) => {\n        if (msg.type !== 'message') log(`hub → ${p.key}: ${msg.type}${msg.type === 'start' ? ` in ${msg.in} ms` : ''}${msg.type === 'leave' ? ` ${msg.id} (${msg.reason})` : ''}${msg.type === 'end' ? ` ${msg.reason}` : ''}`);\n        post(msg);\n      },\n      net: endpoint,\n      onIssue: (i) => log(`${p.key} ✗ ${i.problem}`),\n      onFullscreen: (on) => log(`${p.key} asked for fullscreen ${on ? 'on' : 'off'}: the hub's page takes it`),\n      onAnswer: (what) => answerCard(state, cell, what),\n      // The scoreboard's feed: this cell's own progress, as its bridge passes it on.\n      onProgress: (id, report) => {\n        if (id !== cell.bridge?.me) return;\n        cell.progress.push({ at: performance.now(), ...report });\n        state.coordinator.progress(id, report.score);\n        render(state);\n      },\n    });\n    endpoint.onMessage((from, env) => cell.bridge.fromNet(from, env));\n    cell.detach = attachFrame(frame, (msg) => cell.bridge.fromGame(msg));\n    frame.addEventListener('load', () => instrument(cell), { once: true });\n    frame.src = gameUrl(game, { tag: metas?.mode, seed });\n    state.cells.push(cell);\n  }\n  renderWho(state);\n  render(state);\n  // By hand, the card lifts by itself after ten seconds (more when a player asks), as in a session;\n  // the conformance run releases it itself.\n  const ticker = setInterval(() => {\n    if (state !== current || state.coordinator.released) return clearInterval(ticker);\n    if (!auto && performance.now() >= state.splashUntil) return releaseRound(state);\n    tickCard(state);\n  }, 250);\n  return state;\n}\n\nfunction releaseRound(state = current) {\n  if (!state || state !== current || state.coordinator.released) return;\n  state.splashUntil = null;\n  tickCard(state);\n  log('splash over: the round starts once every game has loaded');\n  state.coordinator.release();\n}\n\n/** A game's own card, as the hub drives it: the countdown and who is ready, to every copy that shows one. */\nfunction tickCard(state) {\n  const left = state.splashUntil === null ? null : Math.max(0, state.splashUntil - performance.now());\n  const ready = state.cells.filter((c) => state.answers.ready.has(c.key)).map((c) => c.bridge.me);\n  for (const cell of state.cells) {\n    if (cell.gone || !cell.bridge.showsCard) continue;\n    const card = { left, paused: false, starting: left === null, ready, asking: state.answers.more.size, asked: state.answers.more.has(cell.key) };\n    const id = JSON.stringify({ ...card, left: left === null ? null : Math.ceil(left / 1000) });\n    if (cell.cardSent === id) continue;\n    cell.cardSent = id;\n    cell.bridge.card(card);\n  }\n}\n\n/** A player answered on the game's own card: Ready, or more time (+10 s; again takes it back). */\nfunction answerCard(state, cell, what) {\n  if (state !== current || state.coordinator.released || cell.server) return;\n  const { ready, more } = state.answers;\n  if (what === 'ready') {\n    ready.add(cell.key);\n    more.delete(cell.key);\n  } else if (more.has(cell.key)) {\n    more.delete(cell.key);\n  } else {\n    more.add(cell.key);\n    ready.delete(cell.key);\n    state.splashUntil += 10_000;\n  }\n  log(`${cell.key} answers ${what} on the game's card`);\n  const players = state.cells.filter((c) => !c.server && !c.gone);\n  if (!auto && players.every((c) => ready.has(c.key))) return releaseRound(state);\n  tickCard(state);\n}\n\nfunction endCurrent() {\n  if (!current) return;\n  current.coordinator.abort('session-ended');\n  for (const cell of current.cells) removeCell(cell, false);\n  current.hubEnd.close();\n  current = null;\n}\n\nfunction removeCell(cell, tellRound = true) {\n  if (cell.gone) return;\n  cell.gone = true;\n  cell.detach();\n  cell.endpoint.close();\n  cell.frame.remove();\n  cell.el.classList.add('is-out');\n  if (tellRound) {\n    log(`${cell.key} left`);\n    current?.coordinator.leave(cell.key, 'left');\n  }\n}\n\nfunction renderWho(state) {\n  $('who').replaceChildren(...state.cells.map((c) => new Option(`${c.name} (${c.key})${c.server ? ' — host, no player' : c.slot === 0 && !serverMode ? ' — host' : ''}`, c.key)));\n}\n\nfunction render(state) {\n  const s = state.status;\n  if (!s) return;\n  for (const cell of state.cells) {\n    const p = s.players.find((q) => q.key === cell.key) ?? (s.server?.key === cell.key ? s.server : null);\n    if (!p) continue;\n    const bits = [];\n    if (p.out) bits.push(`out: ${p.out}`);\n    else if (p.result) bits.push(`result ${JSON.stringify(p.result)}`);\n    else if (p.ready) bits.push('ready');\n    else if (p.hello) bits.push('welcomed');\n    else bits.push('loading');\n    const last = cell.progress.at(-1);\n    if (last && !p.result) bits.push(`progress ${last.score}${last.label ? ` (${last.label})` : ''}`);\n    bits.push(`↑${cell.bridge.stats.sent} ↓${cell.bridge.stats.received}`);\n    cell.label.querySelector('.cell__state').textContent = bits.join(' · ');\n    cell.el.classList.toggle('is-out', !!p.out || cell.gone);\n  }\n  const lines = [`Round ${s.round} · ${s.mode || 'mode unknown'} · phase ${s.phase}`, `Host: ${s.server ? 'the server, no player' : `player ${s.host}`} · seed ${state.seed}`];\n  if (s.gate && !s.released) lines.push(`Card: ${state.cells.some((c) => c.bridge.showsCard) ? 'the game’s own, ' : ''}${state.splashUntil ? `${Math.max(0, Math.ceil((state.splashUntil - performance.now()) / 1000))} s left` : 'held'} (Start now ends it)`);\n  if (state.record) {\n    const name = (id) => s.players[id]?.name ?? `#${id}`;\n    lines.push(`Ended ${state.record.status} (${state.record.reason})`);\n    if (state.record.standings) state.record.standings.forEach((ids, i) => lines.push(`  ${i + 1}. ${ids.map(name).join(', ')}`));\n  }\n  if (s.issues.length) lines.push(...s.issues.map((i) => `✗ ${i.key}: ${i.problem}`));\n  $('round').textContent = lines.join('\\n');\n}\n\n$('restart').onclick = () => newRound();\n$('release').onclick = () => releaseRound();\n$('timeup').onclick = () => current?.coordinator.timeUp();\n$('remove').onclick = () => {\n  const cell = current?.cells.find((c) => c.key === $('who').value);\n  if (cell) removeCell(cell);\n};\n$('hide').onclick = () => {\n  if (!current) return;\n  current.hidden = !current.hidden;\n  $('hide').setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(current.hidden));\n  (current.cells.find((c) => c.server) ?? current.cells[0])?.bridge.visibility(current.hidden);\n  log(`host tab ${current.hidden ? 'hidden' : 'shown'}`);\n};\nfor (const id of ['latency', 'jitter', 'loss']) $(id).onchange = applyNet;\n\n/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n * ?auto=1 — the conformance run. It presses keys inside each frame with\n * synthetic events while the round plays (the frames must be served from this\n * page's origin). Results land in window.__hubCheck, and body[data-complete]\n * turns \"true\".\n * ------------------------------------------------------------------------- */\n\nconst sleep = (ms) => new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, ms));\nasync function until(test, ms) {\n  const end = performance.now() + ms;\n  while (performance.now() < end) {\n    if (test()) return true;\n    await sleep(50);\n  }\n  return test();\n}\n\nfunction poke(cell, key) {\n  const doc = cell.frame.contentDocument;\n  const win = cell.frame.contentWindow;\n  if (!doc || !win) return false;\n  const target = doc.activeElement && doc.activeElement !== doc.documentElement ? doc.activeElement : doc.body || doc.documentElement;\n  const init = { key, code: key === ' ' ? 'Space' : key, bubbles: true, cancelable: true, view: win };\n  target.dispatchEvent(new win.KeyboardEvent('keydown', init));\n  setTimeout(() => target.dispatchEvent(new win.KeyboardEvent('keyup', init)), 120);\n  return true;\n}\n\nasync function conformance() {\n  const checks = [];\n  const check = (name, pass, detail = '') => {\n    checks.push({ name, pass: !!pass, detail });\n    renderChecks(checks);\n    return !!pass;\n  };\n  const report = { done: false, pass: false, game: $('game').value, players: Number($('players').value), scenario, checks, log: logLines };\n  window.__hubCheck = report;\n  try {\n    const state = await newRound();\n    if (!state) {\n      check('game named', false, 'pass ?game=<path> of a page on this site');\n      return;\n    }\n    const n = state.n;\n    const m = state.metas;\n    check('head metas', m && m.session === '1' && modeOf(m.mode), m ? `hub:session=${m.session} mode=${m.mode}` : 'could not fetch the page');\n    const seats = String(m?.players ?? '').match(/\\d+/g)?.map(Number) ?? [];\n    const [least, most = least] = seats;\n    check('hub:session-players is a range within 1–4', seats.length >= 1 && seats.length <= 2 && least >= 1 && least <= most && most <= 4, `hub:session-players=${m?.players}`);\n    if (m?.minutes != null) check('hub:session-minutes, when given, is a number', Number(m.minutes) > 0, `hub:session-minutes=${m.minutes}`);\n\n    // Every copy: the players, and in a server round the server's copy.\n    const copies = () => [...(state.status?.players ?? []), ...(state.status?.server ? [state.status.server] : [])];\n    const helloed = await until(() => copies().every((p) => p.hello), TIMINGS.helloMs + 1000);\n    check('every copy says hello', helloed, copies().filter((p) => !p.hello).map((p) => p.key).join(', '));\n    if (!helloed) return;\n    const caps = state.coordinator.seats().map((s) => s.caps);\n    check('hello names protocol 1 and the mode', caps.every((c) => c.v === 1 && modeOf(c.mode) === state.coordinator.mode), JSON.stringify(caps[0]));\n    check('hello seats cover this player count', caps.every((c) => Array.isArray(c.seats) && c.seats[0] <= Math.max(2, n) && c.seats[1] >= n), JSON.stringify(caps[0]?.seats));\n    if (state.cells.some((c) => !c.frame.contentDocument)) {\n      check('frames reachable for synthetic input', false, 'serve the game from the same origin as this harness');\n      return;\n    }\n\n    // The card collects ready: every game readies up by itself once loaded, with no prompt and no key.\n    const loaded = await until(() => copies().every((p) => p.ready), 20_000);\n    check('ready without a key press (the card asks the players)', loaded, copies().filter((p) => !p.ready).map((p) => p.key).join(', '));\n    // A game that shows its own card takes the players' answers on it: Enter is Ready.\n    if (caps.some((c) => c?.card)) {\n      const players = state.cells.filter((c) => !c.server);\n      const sent = await until(() => players.every((c) => c.cardSent), 2000);\n      for (const cell of players) poke(cell, 'Enter');\n      const answered = await until(() => players.every((c) => state.answers.ready.has(c.key)), 3000);\n      check('its own card: Enter answers Ready', sent && answered, players.filter((c) => !state.answers.ready.has(c.key)).map((c) => `${c.key}${c.cardSent ? '' : ' (no card yet)'}`).join(', '));\n    }\n    releaseRound(state);\n    const started = await until(() => state.status?.phase !== 'loading', 15_000);\n    check('the round starts when the card ends', started && copies().every((p) => p.ready), copies().filter((p) => !p.ready).map((p) => p.key).join(', ') || state.status?.phase);\n    if (!started || state.record) return;\n\n    await until(() => state.status.phase === 'playing' || state.record, TIMINGS.countdownMs + 2000);\n    const arrows = ['ArrowLeft', 'ArrowRight', 'ArrowUp', 'ArrowDown', 'a', 'd', 'w', 's'];\n    const randomly = async (ms) => {\n      const end = performance.now() + ms;\n      while (performance.now() < end && !state.record) {\n        for (const cell of state.cells) if (!cell.gone && !cell.server) poke(cell, arrows[Math.floor(Math.random() * arrows.length)]);\n        await sleep(150);\n      }\n    };\n    await randomly(Math.min(1500, playMs / 4));\n\n    const mode = state.coordinator.mode;\n    // Parallel and ghost: every copy runs its own world from the same seeded start. A game\n    // still tagged race was built to race's contract: no seeded start, and no progress asked.\n    const own = SELF_REPORTED.includes(mode);\n    const legacyRace = own && !seedsRandom(m?.mode);\n    if (own && !legacyRace) {\n      const seeded = state.cells.every((c) => c.frame.contentWindow?.AIHub?.seeded === true);\n      check(`${mode}: Math.random is seeded, the same on every copy`, seeded, state.cells.map((c) => `${c.key}: client ${c.frame.contentWindow?.AIHub?.version ?? '?'} seeded ${c.frame.contentWindow?.AIHub?.seeded}`).join('; '));\n    }\n\n    if (scenario === 'host-leave') removeCell(state.cells[0]);\n    else if (n >= 3) removeCell(state.cells[n - 1]);\n    await randomly(playMs / 2);\n    const remaining = state.cells.filter((c) => !c.gone);\n    if (own) {\n      if (mode === 'parallel') {\n        check('parallel: no game traffic', state.cells.every((c) => c.bridge.stats.sent === 0),\n          state.cells.map((c) => `${c.key} ↑${c.bridge.stats.sent}`).join(' '));\n      } else {\n        check('ghost: every copy sends its player', remaining.every((c) => c.bridge.stats.sent > 0) || n === 1,\n          remaining.map((c) => `${c.key} ↑${c.bridge.stats.sent}`).join(' '));\n      }\n      if (!legacyRace) check(`${mode}: every copy reports its progress`, remaining.every((c) => c.progress.length > 0 || state.status?.players.find((p) => p.key === c.key)?.result),\n        remaining.map((c) => `${c.key}: ${c.progress.length} report${c.progress.length === 1 ? '' : 's'}`).join(', '));\n    } else {\n      check('game traffic flows both ways', remaining.every((c) => c.bridge.stats.sent > 0 && c.bridge.stats.received > 0) || n === 1,\n        remaining.map((c) => `${c.key} ↑${c.bridge.stats.sent} ↓${c.bridge.stats.received}`).join(' '));\n    }\n\n    if (!state.record) state.coordinator.timeUp();\n    const ended = await until(() => state.record, TIMINGS.graceMs + 2000);\n    const record = state.record;\n    if (serverMode) {\n      // The world ran on the server: the players heard it, and only the host may finish a shared world.\n      const serverCell = state.cells.find((c) => c.server);\n      check('a copy with no player of its own runs the world (as a server would)', ended && record.status === 'played' && record.hostId === serverCell.bridge.me && serverCell.bridge.stats.sent > 0,\n        record ? `${record.status} (${record.reason}), host ${record.hostId}, server sent ${serverCell.bridge.stats.sent}` : 'no end');\n    }\n    if (scenario === 'host-leave' && !SELF_REPORTED.includes(state.coordinator.mode)) {\n      check('host leaving voids the round', ended && record.status === 'void' && record.endReason === 'host-left', record ? `${record.status} (${record.reason})` : 'no end');\n    } else {\n      check('the round ends with a valid result', ended && record.status === 'played', record ? `${record.status} (${record.reason})` : 'no end within the grace period');\n    }\n    await sleep(300);\n    check('every remaining copy is told the round ended', remaining.every((c) => c.bridge.ended), remaining.filter((c) => !c.bridge.ended).map((c) => c.key).join(', '));\n    const issues = [...(state.status?.issues ?? []), ...state.cells.flatMap((c) => c.bridge.issues)];\n    check('no protocol problems', issues.length === 0, issues.map((i) => `${i.key}: ${i.problem}`).join('; '));\n    const violations = state.cells.flatMap((c) => {\n      let extra = [];\n      try {\n        extra = c.frame.contentWindow?.__hubViolations ?? [];\n      } catch {}\n      return [...c.violations, ...extra].map((v) => `${c.key}: ${v}`);\n    });\n    check('no errors, dialogs, popups or sockets', violations.length === 0, violations.slice(0, 6).join('; '));\n  } catch (error) {\n    check('harness ran', false, String(error?.stack || error));\n  } finally {\n    report.pass = checks.length > 0 && checks.every((c) => c.pass);\n    report.done = true;\n    document.body.dataset.complete = 'true';\n    log(`conformance: ${report.pass ? 'PASS' : 'FAIL'}`);\n  }\n}\n\nfunction renderChecks(checks) {\n  $('checklist').replaceChildren(\n    ...checks.map((c) => {\n      const li = document.createElement('li');\n      li.className = c.pass ? 'ok' : 'bad';\n      li.textContent = c.name + (c.detail && !c.pass ? ` — ${c.detail}` : '');\n      li.title = c.detail;\n      return li;\n    }),\n  );\n}\n\nif (auto) conformance();\nelse if ($('game').value) newRound();\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>\n","numLines":549,"startLine":1,"totalLines":549}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01ErYhCY2XXKM5RddJjRcb19","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgj94jUQF7t4BJUZow2Lo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LLwf8Y6jJqrREiCp4i5yRB","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211959__x9a5b1d/work/_research/engine/x/pixel-engine/ASSETS.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":40534,"cache_read_input_tokens":32799,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":40534},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4a882869-9e92-4155-a3b0-121d8fdc660c","uuid":"86b0c988-123e-455b-bf7c-1466568652cb","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:20:58.137Z","request_id":"req_011Cgj94jDX2ZjgqqU65JK6V","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01LLwf8Y6jJqrREiCp4i5yRB":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211959__x9a5b1d/work/_research/engine/x/pixel-engine/ASSETS.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LLwf8Y6jJqrREiCp4i5yRB","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Pixel Engine: models and textures\n2\t\n3\t> Pixel Engine **0.46.0**, build 2026-11-02 f75d4a6. Read `GUIDE.md` first. `LIBRARY.md` lists the built-in models and textures, `CREDITS.md` where they came from.\n4\t\n5\tFor an agent building a game on the kit; read `GUIDE.md` first. Objects and pixel-art textures\n6\tare **plain data** you write, check and look at, then fix: a `ModelDef` of keyed primitives that\n7\tthe engine turns into toon meshes, a `TextureDef` of layers it bakes into texels. No modelling\n8\ttool and no image files. `LIBRARY.md` lists the built-in models and textures and the imported\n9\tpacks (`library.json` holds the same as data), `check.mjs --sheets` draws what you write, and `examples/market.html` is a scene built this way\n10\t(section 6). Every name here comes from `./pixel-engine.js`; `API.md` has the signatures.\n11\t\n12\tContents: 1 The loop · 2 Models · 3 Textures · 4 Style rules · 5 In a game · 6 The example ·\n13\t7 Credits\n14\t\n15\t## 1. The loop\n16\t\n17\t1. **Start from the library.** Search `LIBRARY.md` (by family, then each pack; id, size, params,\n18\t   palette slots, tags, one row each, a model's variants like `rock-large-a` … `-f` sharing\n19\t   one), filter `library.json`, or search in code:\n20\t   `MODEL_LIBRARY.search('wooden chair')` ranks id words over tags over `about`, plurals and\n21\t   parts of words included; `MODEL_LIBRARY.get('fence')` takes an id. Place library models as\n22\t   they are, re-coloured or with other params, and `use` them inside your own: a stall with\n23\t   crates is a few lines.\n24\t2. **Write** your defs in a module of their own (`models.js`) that exports them; the game\n25\t   imports it. Keep the engine start out of that module.\n26\t3. **Check and look:** `node check.mjs --sheets models.js` draws a sheet of every def the module\n27\t   exports (by name, in an array or object, or in a catalog: `check/sheets/<id>.png`; textures\n28\t   `<id>.tex.png`) and prints its problems and warnings; it exits 1 on a problem. **Open the\n29\t   PNGs.** `--sheets fence,cobbles` draws library ids: look at one before you place it.\n30\t4. **Fix** the numbers the messages and the sheet point at, and run it again until there is no\n31\t   problem and the game-scale previews read. Warnings name what won't read at 480×270: fix them\n32\t   unless you mean it.\n33\t5. **Look in the game:** `node check.mjs index.html --cameras`, then the PNGs: the real\n34\t   renderer, with lights and looks.\n35\t\n36\tIn code, `checkModel(def, { catalog })` and `validateTexture(def)` return\n37\t`{ problems, warnings }`, and `modelSheet(def, { catalog })` and `textureSheet(def)` return the\n38\tsheet as RGBA pixels (`image`) with them.\n39\t\n40\t| sheet row | answers |\n41\t| --- | --- |\n42\t| turntable, 8 angles at one scale | Is the silhouette right from every side? |\n43\t| front / side / top on a 0.1 m grid, with the size in metres | Are the parts where the numbers say? Do they touch? Is it the right size? |\n44\t| game scale: an iso camera (yaw 45°, pitch 42°) at about 19 and 22 pixels a metre, one art pixel per pixel, ×4 | Does it read in a game? (The engine's iso camera at zoom 1 shows about 20.) |\n45\t| palette, check | Which slots, which colours, which are unused; the problems and warnings, each naming the part and the fix |\n46\t\n47\tSheets are drawn in software (three shading bands, outlines) without point lights or looks: the\n48\tgame is the truth.\n49\t\n50\t## 2. Models\n51\t\n52\t```js\n53\texport const crate = model({\n54\t  id: 'crate',\n55\t  about: 'Wooden crate with a frame and diagonal braces', // one line: find() searches it\n56\t  tags: ['container', 'wood'],\n57\t  palette: { wood: 'orange', band: 'red' }, // slots → the 16 palette names (GUIDE.md section 4)\n58\t  parts: [\n59\t    { box: [0.68, 0.68, 0.68], at: [0, 0.36, 0], c: 'wood' },\n60\t    boxFrame({ size: [0.72, 0.72, 0.72], beam: 0.09, at: [0, 0.36, 0], c: 'band' }),\n61\t    { mirror: [{ box: [0.8, 0.08, 0.04], at: [0, 0.36, 0.35], rot: [0, 0, 45], c: 'band' }], axis: 'z' },\n62\t  ],\n63\t});\n64\t```\n65\t\n66\tMetres and degrees; +Y is up, +Z is the front, the floor is y = 0. Parts are keyed, never\n67\tpositional. **Every primitive fills its box `[w, h, d]`, centred on `at`**, turned by `rot` (XYZ,\n68\tabout `at`), and round kinds stretch to it:\n69\t\n70\t- `box`; `cyl` (an n-sided prism, `seg` sides, default 6 to 10 by size; `top`: the top width ÷\n71\t  the bottom width); `cone` (point up); `ball` (`half`: the upper dome); `lump` (a rock, `seed`);\n72\t  `wedge` (a ramp, full height at the back, −Z); `torus` (a ring in XZ as thick as the box is tall).\n73\t- Profile kinds use their own coordinates, placed at `at`: `lathe` ((radius, height) points\n74\t  turned about Y), `slab` (an XY outline or SVG path, extruded `depth` along Z), `tube` (points\n75\t  and a radius `r`, or a pair that tapers).\n76\t- Every part takes `c` (its slot; default the first), `name`, `glow: true` (unlit: a flame's\n77\t  heart, eyes), `tex` (a texture id, section 3), `seg` and `collide: false` (no box of its own\n78\t  under `collider: 'parts'`: a doorway's mortar ring).\n79\t\n80\t**Composition:**\n81\t\n82\t- `{ group: [...], at, rot, scale, c }`: a frame whose `c` is its parts' default. `pivot: true`\n83\t  with a `name` keeps it a movable Group (a door, a lid: `build.object.getObjectByName('lid')`).\n84\t- `{ mirror: [...], axis: 'x' }`: the parts and their mirror image (`axis: 'z'` mirrors front to back).\n85\t- `{ use: 'barrel', at, rot, scale, params, seed, palette: { theirs: 'ours' } }`: another model\n86\t  by id. Its slots map onto yours through `palette`, else onto yours of the same name, else keep\n87\t  their own colours.\n88\t- `on: 'name'`: sit on the named part's top; `at` becomes an offset from there.\n89\t- `params: { h: [default, min, max] }` with `parts: (p, rng) => [...]`: parametric (`p.h`) and\n90\t  seeded (`rng.range(a, b)`). Helpers return parts: `around`, `rowOf`, `gridOf`, `scatterOf`,\n91\t  `boxFrame`.\n92\t- Model keys: `size` (declared bounds, checked), `anchors` (`{ grip: [x, y, z] }`), `light: { at,\n93\t  c, intensity, radius, flicker }`, `collider` (`'box'`, `'cyl'`, `'hull'`, `'parts'` (a box per\n94\t  part: doorways stay open) or `'none'`), `floats: true` (it hangs), `texel` (texels a metre for\n95\t  `tex` parts, default 8).\n96\t\n97\t**Problems** (`check.mjs --sheets` exits 1; `buildModel` throws a `ModelError` on those it can't\n98\tbuild): no `about` or `tags`; an undeclared slot or a colour that isn't a palette name; an unknown\n99\t`use`, `on` or texture; a size that isn't positive; `seg` outside 3–64; NaN; an empty model; below\n100\tthe floor (unless `floats`); over the declared `size`; params out of range; a part that both\n101\tglows and takes a `tex`; a `texel` outside 2–64. **Warnings:** a part floating more than 1 cm from the\n102\trest; rods under 0.06 m; over the triangle budget (300 under 0.5 m across, 1,000 under 2 m, else\n103\t3,000); over 8 materials; a part hidden inside another; coplanar faces of two colours; touching big\n104\tmasses too close in lightness; one colour over 40% of the model in four or more parts; glow over\n105\t15% of it. `checkModel` builds the defaults, every param at its min and at its max, and three\n106\tseeds when the parts read `rng`.\n107\t\n108\t## 3. Textures\n109\t\n110\t```js\n111\texport const bricks = textureDef({\n112\t  id: 'bricks',\n113\t  about: 'Stone bricks in courses over dark mortar',\n114\t  tags: ['stone', 'wall', 'surface'],\n115\t  size: [16, 16], // texels; powers of two when it tiles\n116\t  tile: true, // seamless: patterns wrap\n117\t  palette: { mortar: 'night', stone: 'slate', stone2: 'mist' },\n118\t  layers: [{ pattern: 'bricks', colors: ['mortar', 'stone', 'stone2'], w: 8, h: 4, seed: 2 }],\n119\t});\n120\t```\n121\t\n122\t**Layers** draw in order: `{ pixels: [...rows], legend: { k: 'slot' } }` (`.` or a space is clear;\n123\t`at`, `mirror: 'x'` or `'y'`), `{ pattern, colors, seed, dither, ...params }` (over a ramp of\n124\tslots, dark to light), `{ path: 'M … Z', fill, stroke }` (SVG in texel units) and `{ outline:\n125\tslot }`. `frames: n` makes a strip of n frames, left to right.\n126\t\n127\t**Patterns:** `noise bricks tiles planks cobbles stripes checker scatter cracks gradient`.\n128\tParameters: noise `scale`, `octaves`; bricks and tiles `w`, `h`, `mortar`, `offset`, `bevel`;\n129\tplanks `w`, `gap`, `length`, `grain`; cobbles `cells`, `gap`; stripes `width`, `dir`; checker\n130\t`cell`; scatter `count`, `size`, `shape`; cracks `count`, `length`; gradient `dir`. A problem\n131\tnames the range of a bad one.\n132\t\n133\t**Density:** surfaces at 8 texels a metre (`DEFAULT_TEXEL`); denser ones shimmer as the camera\n134\tzooms. A 16-texel tile covers 2 m, so draw a brick of 8 × 4 texels for 1 × 0.5 m. **Warnings:** a\n135\tseam across the wrap, salt and pepper (over 15% single texels), a tiling size that isn't a power\n136\tof two, unused slots.\n137\t\n138\t## 4. Style rules\n139\t\n140\t- **Scale:** the hero is 1.6 m (1.75 m with the cap); a door 2.2 m, a table 0.75 m, a chair seat 0.45 m.\n141\t- **Silhouette first.** The iso camera sees the top and two sides: big masses must read; put\n142\t  detail on the top and the front.\n143\t- **Thickness:** 0.06 m at least; 0.12 m or more for parts that carry the silhouette.\n144\t- **Colour separates parts:** touching parts take different colours or shades (planks and their\n145\t  frame, stones and mortar), up to 8, one an accent; touching big masses differ in lightness.\n146\t- **Glow is flat:** keep it for small hot spots. For fire `use: 'flame'`, and never turn it about\n147\t  Y: its tongues face the camera. Below `h` 0.5 its 2–4 tongues read as a dark smudge: use\n148\t  `tongues: 1` for small fires.\n149\t- **Low poly:** 6 to 10 sides on round kinds, no bevels under 2 cm.\n150\t- **Grounded:** the base on y = 0, nothing floating unless `floats`.\n151\t- **Compose before you create:** `use` a library model before you write a new crate.\n152\t\n153\t## 5. In a game\n154\t\n155\t- `buildModel(idOrDef, { params, seed, palette, light, catalog, textures })` returns `object`\n156\t  (one merged mesh per material; pivots are named Groups), `bounds`, `anchors`, `colliders`\n157\t  (data: `addModelColliders(physics, build, at, yaw)`), `light` (in model space: place it with\n158\t  the model, as the example does) and `report`. Builds whose parts don't read `rng` are cached and\n159\t  share geometry: place as many as you like.\n160\t- **Your own models:** a `ModelCatalog` of the library and yours, passed as `catalog` (or\n161\t  `MODEL_LIBRARY.add(def)`); your own textures likewise in a `TextureCatalog`, passed as `textures`.\n162\t- **Textures:** `toonMaterial(PALETTE.white, { map: textureMap('bricks') })` on any mesh (the\n163\t  map is cached and shared: scale UVs, never the map); `new SpriteBatch(spriteSheet('coin-spin'),\n164\t  { capacity: 64 })`; `hudSprite('gem-icon')` gives rows and colours for `ctx.hud.sprite`.\n165\t- **Packs** (`packs/`, listed in `packs/index.json` and LIBRARY.md): kits by other artists,\n166\t  imported into this format and palette. `const kit = await loadPack('packs/<id>.json',\n167\t  { textures: TEXTURE_LIBRARY })`, then `buildModel('<id>/<name>', { catalog: kit })`; its\n168\t  textures then work by id like the library's. `kit.search('tree')` searches the pack. To vary\n169\t  one of its models, load the pack into your catalog (`loadPack(url, { into: MODEL_LIBRARY })`)\n170\t  and add a def there that `use`s it with a `scale` or a `palette`: nothing is copied.\n171\t\n172\t## 6. The example\n173\t\n174\tMarket Corner, the kit's `examples/market.html`: library models (one re-coloured, three with\n175\tparams, the lamp post's light made brighter), a cobbled floor from `textureMap`, and a stall of\n176\tthe game's own in a module of its own. `node check.mjs examples/market.html` plays it;\n177\t`node check.mjs --sheets examples/market-models.js` draws its stall.\n178\t\n179\t```js market-models\n180\t// Market Corner's own models: plain data in a module of their own, so `node check.mjs --sheets\n181\t// examples/market-models.js` can draw them.\n182\timport { model, MODEL_LIBRARY, ModelCatalog } from './pixel-engine.js';\n183\t\n184\texport const fruitStall = model({\n185\t  id: 'fruit-stall',\n186\t  about: 'The market stall under a green awning, two baskets of fruit on its counter',\n187\t  tags: ['town', 'market'],\n188\t  palette: { wood: 'orange', cloth: 'green', cloth2: 'white', top: 'sand', basket: 'red', fruit: 'orange', fruit2: 'lime' },\n189\t  parts: [\n190\t    { use: 'market-stall' }, // its slots take ours of the same name: the awning turns green\n191\t    ...[-0.45, 0.4].flatMap((x, i) => [\n192\t      { name: `basket${i}`, cyl: [0.56, 0.14, 0.4], at: [x, 1.01, 0.05], top: 1.25, c: 'basket' },\n193\t      ...[-0.17, 0, 0.17].map((dx, k) => ({ ball: [0.18, 0.18, 0.18], on: `basket${i}`, at: [dx, 0, 0], c: (i + k) % 2 ? 'fruit2' : 'fruit' })),\n194\t    ]),\n195\t  ],\n196\t});\n197\t\n198\t// Where the game's ids resolve: the library and ours (buildModel's `catalog`).\n199\texport const MODELS = new ModelCatalog([...MODEL_LIBRARY.all(), fruitStall]);\n200\t```\n201\t\n202\t```js market\n203\t// Market Corner: library models and the game's own fruit stall on a cobbled square at dusk.\n204\t// Nothing to play: a scene to look at, and to build yours from (ASSETS.md).\n205\timport { addModelColliders, buildModel, DEFAULT_TEXEL, Engine, hudSprite, PALETTE, TEXTURE_LIBRARY, textureMap, THREE, toonMaterial, withUrlOptions } from './pixel-engine.js';\n206\timport { MODELS } from './market-models.js';\n207\t\n208\tconst { Color, Mesh, PlaneGeometry, Vector3 } = THREE;\n209\t\n210\t// [id, position, options]: buildModel's options (params, palette, seed, light) and a turn in degrees\n211\tconst SCENE = [\n212\t  ['fruit-stall', [0, 0, -1.4]], // ours (market-models.js)\n213\t  ['market-stall', [-4, 0, 0.6], { turn: 90, palette: { cloth: 'blue' } }], // re-coloured\n214\t  ['lamp-post', [1, 0, 1.6], { light: { intensity: 10 } }], // it carries a light: brighter\n215\t  ['well', [3.8, 0, -2.2]],\n216\t  ['fence', [-0.5, 0, -3.4], { params: { length: 7 } }],\n217\t  ['barrel', [-1.8, 0, 1.2]],\n218\t  ['crate', [-1.1, 0, 1.7], { turn: 20 }],\n219\t  ['sack', [2.4, 0, 1], { params: { h: 0.6 } }],\n220\t  ['oak', [-3.2, 0, -3.4], { params: { h: 3 }, seed: 2 }],\n221\t];\n222\t\n223\tclass MarketCorner {\n224\t  name = 'Market Corner';\n225\t  placed = [];\n226\t  lights = [];\n227\t  target = new Vector3(-0.3, 1, -0.9);\n228\t\n229\t  setup(ctx) {\n230\t    const { scene, physics, engine } = ctx;\n231\t    engine.sun.intensity = 1.4; // dusk, so the lamp shows (the engine resets it for the next game)\n232\t    engine.ambient.color.setHex(PALETTE.navy);\n233\t    scene.background = new Color(PALETTE.night);\n234\t\n235\t    // The floor: a library surface on a plain mesh. A 32-texel tile at 8 texels a metre covers\n236\t    // 4 m, so the UVs count tiles (the map is cached and shared: never scale it).\n237\t    const tile = TEXTURE_LIBRARY.get('cobbles').size[0] / DEFAULT_TEXEL;\n238\t    const ground = new PlaneGeometry(16, 16).rotateX(-Math.PI / 2);\n239\t    ground.attributes.uv.array.forEach((v, i, uv) => (uv[i] = (v * 16) / tile));\n240\t    const floor = new Mesh(ground, toonMaterial(PALETTE.white, { map: textureMap('cobbles') }));\n241\t    floor.receiveShadow = true;\n242\t    scene.add(floor);\n243\t    physics.addStaticBox({ position: [0, -0.5, 0], halfExtents: [8, 0.5, 8] });\n244\t\n245\t    for (const [id, at, { turn = 0, ...options } = {}] of SCENE) {\n246\t      const m = buildModel(id, { ...options, catalog: MODELS });\n247\t      m.object.position.set(...at);\n248\t      m.object.rotation.y = (turn * Math.PI) / 180;\n249\t      m.object.updateMatrixWorld();\n250\t      scene.add(m.object);\n251\t      addModelColliders(physics, m, at, m.object.rotation.y);\n252\t      // a model's light is in its own space: place it with the model\n253\t      if (m.light) this.lights.push(ctx.lights.request({ ...m.light, position: m.object.localToWorld(new Vector3(...m.light.at)) }));\n254\t      this.placed.push(m);\n255\t    }\n256\t    this.icon = hudSprite('gold-icon');\n257\t  }\n258\t\n259\t  update(ctx) {\n260\t    ctx.hud.clear();\n261\t    ctx.hud.sprite(6, 6, this.icon.rows, this.icon.colors);\n262\t    ctx.hud.text(26, 10, 'MARKET CORNER', { color: 'sand' });\n263\t  }\n264\t\n265\t  cameraTarget() {\n266\t    return this.target;\n267\t  }\n268\t\n269\t  status() {\n270\t    return `market: ${this.placed.length} models, ${this.lights.length} light`;\n271\t  }\n272\t}\n273\t\n274\tawait Engine.start(new MarketCorner(), withUrlOptions({ container: document.getElementById('app'), camera: { preset: 'iso', zoom: 1.6 } }));\n275\t```\n276\t\n277\t## 7. Credits\n278\t\n279\t`CREDITS.md` says where everything the kit carries came from: the library and the built-in\n280\tmodels are the engine's own work, three.js and Rapier ship under their licences (their texts are\n281\tin it), and each pack's author and licence with every id it holds. Ship it with your game. A def\n282\tyou import or copy from someone else records it in `source: { url, licence, author }`; credit it\n283\tas its licence asks.\n284\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4a882869-9e92-4155-a3b0-121d8fdc660c","uuid":"3493edf2-546c-41eb-b71b-080595676745","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:20:58.146Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211959__x9a5b1d/work/_research/engine/x/pixel-engine/ASSETS.md","content":"# Pixel Engine: models and textures\n\n> Pixel Engine **0.46.0**, build 2026-11-02 f75d4a6. Read `GUIDE.md` first. `LIBRARY.md` lists the built-in models and textures, `CREDITS.md` where they came from.\n\nFor an agent building a game on the kit; read `GUIDE.md` first. Objects and pixel-art textures\nare **plain data** you write, check and look at, then fix: a `ModelDef` of keyed primitives that\nthe engine turns into toon meshes, a `TextureDef` of layers it bakes into texels. No modelling\ntool and no image files. `LIBRARY.md` lists the built-in models and textures and the imported\npacks (`library.json` holds the same as data), `check.mjs --sheets` draws what you write, and `examples/market.html` is a scene built this way\n(section 6). Every name here comes from `./pixel-engine.js`; `API.md` has the signatures.\n\nContents: 1 The loop · 2 Models · 3 Textures · 4 Style rules · 5 In a game · 6 The example ·\n7 Credits\n\n## 1. The loop\n\n1. **Start from the library.** Search `LIBRARY.md` (by family, then each pack; id, size, params,\n   palette slots, tags, one row each, a model's variants like `rock-large-a` … `-f` sharing\n   one), filter `library.json`, or search in code:\n   `MODEL_LIBRARY.search('wooden chair')` ranks id words over tags over `about`, plurals and\n   parts of words included; `MODEL_LIBRARY.get('fence')` takes an id. Place library models as\n   they are, re-coloured or with other params, and `use` them inside your own: a stall with\n   crates is a few lines.\n2. **Write** your defs in a module of their own (`models.js`) that exports them; the game\n   imports it. Keep the engine start out of that module.\n3. **Check and look:** `node check.mjs --sheets models.js` draws a sheet of every def the module\n   exports (by name, in an array or object, or in a catalog: `check/sheets/<id>.png`; textures\n   `<id>.tex.png`) and prints its problems and warnings; it exits 1 on a problem. **Open the\n   PNGs.** `--sheets fence,cobbles` draws library ids: look at one before you place it.\n4. **Fix** the numbers the messages and the sheet point at, and run it again until there is no\n   problem and the game-scale previews read. Warnings name what won't read at 480×270: fix them\n   unless you mean it.\n5. **Look in the game:** `node check.mjs index.html --cameras`, then the PNGs: the real\n   renderer, with lights and looks.\n\nIn code, `checkModel(def, { catalog })` and `validateTexture(def)` return\n`{ problems, warnings }`, and `modelSheet(def, { catalog })` and `textureSheet(def)` return the\nsheet as RGBA pixels (`image`) with them.\n\n| sheet row | answers |\n| --- | --- |\n| turntable, 8 angles at one scale | Is the silhouette right from every side? |\n| front / side / top on a 0.1 m grid, with the size in metres | Are the parts where the numbers say? Do they touch? Is it the right size? |\n| game scale: an iso camera (yaw 45°, pitch 42°) at about 19 and 22 pixels a metre, one art pixel per pixel, ×4 | Does it read in a game? (The engine's iso camera at zoom 1 shows about 20.) |\n| palette, check | Which slots, which colours, which are unused; the problems and warnings, each naming the part and the fix |\n\nSheets are drawn in software (three shading bands, outlines) without point lights or looks: the\ngame is the truth.\n\n## 2. Models\n\n```js\nexport const crate = model({\n  id: 'crate',\n  about: 'Wooden crate with a frame and diagonal braces', // one line: find() searches it\n  tags: ['container', 'wood'],\n  palette: { wood: 'orange', band: 'red' }, // slots → the 16 palette names (GUIDE.md section 4)\n  parts: [\n    { box: [0.68, 0.68, 0.68], at: [0, 0.36, 0], c: 'wood' },\n    boxFrame({ size: [0.72, 0.72, 0.72], beam: 0.09, at: [0, 0.36, 0], c: 'band' }),\n    { mirror: [{ box: [0.8, 0.08, 0.04], at: [0, 0.36, 0.35], rot: [0, 0, 45], c: 'band' }], axis: 'z' },\n  ],\n});\n```\n\nMetres and degrees; +Y is up, +Z is the front, the floor is y = 0. Parts are keyed, never\npositional. **Every primitive fills its box `[w, h, d]`, centred on `at`**, turned by `rot` (XYZ,\nabout `at`), and round kinds stretch to it:\n\n- `box`; `cyl` (an n-sided prism, `seg` sides, default 6 to 10 by size; `top`: the top width ÷\n  the bottom width); `cone` (point up); `ball` (`half`: the upper dome); `lump` (a rock, `seed`);\n  `wedge` (a ramp, full height at the back, −Z); `torus` (a ring in XZ as thick as the box is tall).\n- Profile kinds use their own coordinates, placed at `at`: `lathe` ((radius, height) points\n  turned about Y), `slab` (an XY outline or SVG path, extruded `depth` along Z), `tube` (points\n  and a radius `r`, or a pair that tapers).\n- Every part takes `c` (its slot; default the first), `name`, `glow: true` (unlit: a flame's\n  heart, eyes), `tex` (a texture id, section 3), `seg` and `collide: false` (no box of its own\n  under `collider: 'parts'`: a doorway's mortar ring).\n\n**Composition:**\n\n- `{ group: [...], at, rot, scale, c }`: a frame whose `c` is its parts' default. `pivot: true`\n  with a `name` keeps it a movable Group (a door, a lid: `build.object.getObjectByName('lid')`).\n- `{ mirror: [...], axis: 'x' }`: the parts and their mirror image (`axis: 'z'` mirrors front to back).\n- `{ use: 'barrel', at, rot, scale, params, seed, palette: { theirs: 'ours' } }`: another model\n  by id. Its slots map onto yours through `palette`, else onto yours of the same name, else keep\n  their own colours.\n- `on: 'name'`: sit on the named part's top; `at` becomes an offset from there.\n- `params: { h: [default, min, max] }` with `parts: (p, rng) => [...]`: parametric (`p.h`) and\n  seeded (`rng.range(a, b)`). Helpers return parts: `around`, `rowOf`, `gridOf`, `scatterOf`,\n  `boxFrame`.\n- Model keys: `size` (declared bounds, checked), `anchors` (`{ grip: [x, y, z] }`), `light: { at,\n  c, intensity, radius, flicker }`, `collider` (`'box'`, `'cyl'`, `'hull'`, `'parts'` (a box per\n  part: doorways stay open) or `'none'`), `floats: true` (it hangs), `texel` (texels a metre for\n  `tex` parts, default 8).\n\n**Problems** (`check.mjs --sheets` exits 1; `buildModel` throws a `ModelError` on those it can't\nbuild): no `about` or `tags`; an undeclared slot or a colour that isn't a palette name; an unknown\n`use`, `on` or texture; a size that isn't positive; `seg` outside 3–64; NaN; an empty model; below\nthe floor (unless `floats`); over the declared `size`; params out of range; a part that both\nglows and takes a `tex`; a `texel` outside 2–64. **Warnings:** a part floating more than 1 cm from the\nrest; rods under 0.06 m; over the triangle budget (300 under 0.5 m across, 1,000 under 2 m, else\n3,000); over 8 materials; a part hidden inside another; coplanar faces of two colours; touching big\nmasses too close in lightness; one colour over 40% of the model in four or more parts; glow over\n15% of it. `checkModel` builds the defaults, every param at its min and at its max, and three\nseeds when the parts read `rng`.\n\n## 3. Textures\n\n```js\nexport const bricks = textureDef({\n  id: 'bricks',\n  about: 'Stone bricks in courses over dark mortar',\n  tags: ['stone', 'wall', 'surface'],\n  size: [16, 16], // texels; powers of two when it tiles\n  tile: true, // seamless: patterns wrap\n  palette: { mortar: 'night', stone: 'slate', stone2: 'mist' },\n  layers: [{ pattern: 'bricks', colors: ['mortar', 'stone', 'stone2'], w: 8, h: 4, seed: 2 }],\n});\n```\n\n**Layers** draw in order: `{ pixels: [...rows], legend: { k: 'slot' } }` (`.` or a space is clear;\n`at`, `mirror: 'x'` or `'y'`), `{ pattern, colors, seed, dither, ...params }` (over a ramp of\nslots, dark to light), `{ path: 'M … Z', fill, stroke }` (SVG in texel units) and `{ outline:\nslot }`. `frames: n` makes a strip of n frames, left to right.\n\n**Patterns:** `noise bricks tiles planks cobbles stripes checker scatter cracks gradient`.\nParameters: noise `scale`, `octaves`; bricks and tiles `w`, `h`, `mortar`, `offset`, `bevel`;\nplanks `w`, `gap`, `length`, `grain`; cobbles `cells`, `gap`; stripes `width`, `dir`; checker\n`cell`; scatter `count`, `size`, `shape`; cracks `count`, `length`; gradient `dir`. A problem\nnames the range of a bad one.\n\n**Density:** surfaces at 8 texels a metre (`DEFAULT_TEXEL`); denser ones shimmer as the camera\nzooms. A 16-texel tile covers 2 m, so draw a brick of 8 × 4 texels for 1 × 0.5 m. **Warnings:** a\nseam across the wrap, salt and pepper (over 15% single texels), a tiling size that isn't a power\nof two, unused slots.\n\n## 4. Style rules\n\n- **Scale:** the hero is 1.6 m (1.75 m with the cap); a door 2.2 m, a table 0.75 m, a chair seat 0.45 m.\n- **Silhouette first.** The iso camera sees the top and two sides: big masses must read; put\n  detail on the top and the front.\n- **Thickness:** 0.06 m at least; 0.12 m or more for parts that carry the silhouette.\n- **Colour separates parts:** touching parts take different colours or shades (planks and their\n  frame, stones and mortar), up to 8, one an accent; touching big masses differ in lightness.\n- **Glow is flat:** keep it for small hot spots. For fire `use: 'flame'`, and never turn it about\n  Y: its tongues face the camera. Below `h` 0.5 its 2–4 tongues read as a dark smudge: use\n  `tongues: 1` for small fires.\n- **Low poly:** 6 to 10 sides on round kinds, no bevels under 2 cm.\n- **Grounded:** the base on y = 0, nothing floating unless `floats`.\n- **Compose before you create:** `use` a library model before you write a new crate.\n\n## 5. In a game\n\n- `buildModel(idOrDef, { params, seed, palette, light, catalog, textures })` returns `object`\n  (one merged mesh per material; pivots are named Groups), `bounds`, `anchors`, `colliders`\n  (data: `addModelColliders(physics, build, at, yaw)`), `light` (in model space: place it with\n  the model, as the example does) and `report`. Builds whose parts don't read `rng` are cached and\n  share geometry: place as many as you like.\n- **Your own models:** a `ModelCatalog` of the library and yours, passed as `catalog` (or\n  `MODEL_LIBRARY.add(def)`); your own textures likewise in a `TextureCatalog`, passed as `textures`.\n- **Textures:** `toonMaterial(PALETTE.white, { map: textureMap('bricks') })` on any mesh (the\n  map is cached and shared: scale UVs, never the map); `new SpriteBatch(spriteSheet('coin-spin'),\n  { capacity: 64 })`; `hudSprite('gem-icon')` gives rows and colours for `ctx.hud.sprite`.\n- **Packs** (`packs/`, listed in `packs/index.json` and LIBRARY.md): kits by other artists,\n  imported into this format and palette. `const kit = await loadPack('packs/<id>.json',\n  { textures: TEXTURE_LIBRARY })`, then `buildModel('<id>/<name>', { catalog: kit })`; its\n  textures then work by id like the library's. `kit.search('tree')` searches the pack. To vary\n  one of its models, load the pack into your catalog (`loadPack(url, { into: MODEL_LIBRARY })`)\n  and add a def there that `use`s it with a `scale` or a `palette`: nothing is copied.\n\n## 6. The example\n\nMarket Corner, the kit's `examples/market.html`: library models (one re-coloured, three with\nparams, the lamp post's light made brighter), a cobbled floor from `textureMap`, and a stall of\nthe game's own in a module of its own. `node check.mjs examples/market.html` plays it;\n`node check.mjs --sheets examples/market-models.js` draws its stall.\n\n```js market-models\n// Market Corner's own models: plain data in a module of their own, so `node check.mjs --sheets\n// examples/market-models.js` can draw them.\nimport { model, MODEL_LIBRARY, ModelCatalog } from './pixel-engine.js';\n\nexport const fruitStall = model({\n  id: 'fruit-stall',\n  about: 'The market stall under a green awning, two baskets of fruit on its counter',\n  tags: ['town', 'market'],\n  palette: { wood: 'orange', cloth: 'green', cloth2: 'white', top: 'sand', basket: 'red', fruit: 'orange', fruit2: 'lime' },\n  parts: [\n    { use: 'market-stall' }, // its slots take ours of the same name: the awning turns green\n    ...[-0.45, 0.4].flatMap((x, i) => [\n      { name: `basket${i}`, cyl: [0.56, 0.14, 0.4], at: [x, 1.01, 0.05], top: 1.25, c: 'basket' },\n      ...[-0.17, 0, 0.17].map((dx, k) => ({ ball: [0.18, 0.18, 0.18], on: `basket${i}`, at: [dx, 0, 0], c: (i + k) % 2 ? 'fruit2' : 'fruit' })),\n    ]),\n  ],\n});\n\n// Where the game's ids resolve: the library and ours (buildModel's `catalog`).\nexport const MODELS = new ModelCatalog([...MODEL_LIBRARY.all(), fruitStall]);\n```\n\n```js market\n// Market Corner: library models and the game's own fruit stall on a cobbled square at dusk.\n// Nothing to play: a scene to look at, and to build yours from (ASSETS.md).\nimport { addModelColliders, buildModel, DEFAULT_TEXEL, Engine, hudSprite, PALETTE, TEXTURE_LIBRARY, textureMap, THREE, toonMaterial, withUrlOptions } from './pixel-engine.js';\nimport { MODELS } from './market-models.js';\n\nconst { Color, Mesh, PlaneGeometry, Vector3 } = THREE;\n\n// [id, position, options]: buildModel's options (params, palette, seed, light) and a turn in degrees\nconst SCENE = [\n  ['fruit-stall', [0, 0, -1.4]], // ours (market-models.js)\n  ['market-stall', [-4, 0, 0.6], { turn: 90, palette: { cloth: 'blue' } }], // re-coloured\n  ['lamp-post', [1, 0, 1.6], { light: { intensity: 10 } }], // it carries a light: brighter\n  ['well', [3.8, 0, -2.2]],\n  ['fence', [-0.5, 0, -3.4], { params: { length: 7 } }],\n  ['barrel', [-1.8, 0, 1.2]],\n  ['crate', [-1.1, 0, 1.7], { turn: 20 }],\n  ['sack', [2.4, 0, 1], { params: { h: 0.6 } }],\n  ['oak', [-3.2, 0, -3.4], { params: { h: 3 }, seed: 2 }],\n];\n\nclass MarketCorner {\n  name = 'Market Corner';\n  placed = [];\n  lights = [];\n  target = new Vector3(-0.3, 1, -0.9);\n\n  setup(ctx) {\n    const { scene, physics, engine } = ctx;\n    engine.sun.intensity = 1.4; // dusk, so the lamp shows (the engine resets it for the next game)\n    engine.ambient.color.setHex(PALETTE.navy);\n    scene.background = new Color(PALETTE.night);\n\n    // The floor: a library surface on a plain mesh. A 32-texel tile at 8 texels a metre covers\n    // 4 m, so the UVs count tiles (the map is cached and shared: never scale it).\n    const tile = TEXTURE_LIBRARY.get('cobbles').size[0] / DEFAULT_TEXEL;\n    const ground = new PlaneGeometry(16, 16).rotateX(-Math.PI / 2);\n    ground.attributes.uv.array.forEach((v, i, uv) => (uv[i] = (v * 16) / tile));\n    const floor = new Mesh(ground, toonMaterial(PALETTE.white, { map: textureMap('cobbles') }));\n    floor.receiveShadow = true;\n    scene.add(floor);\n    physics.addStaticBox({ position: [0, -0.5, 0], halfExtents: [8, 0.5, 8] });\n\n    for (const [id, at, { turn = 0, ...options } = {}] of SCENE) {\n      const m = buildModel(id, { ...options, catalog: MODELS });\n      m.object.position.set(...at);\n      m.object.rotation.y = (turn * Math.PI) / 180;\n      m.object.updateMatrixWorld();\n      scene.add(m.object);\n      addModelColliders(physics, m, at, m.object.rotation.y);\n      // a model's light is in its own space: place it with the model\n      if (m.light) this.lights.push(ctx.lights.request({ ...m.light, position: m.object.localToWorld(new Vector3(...m.light.at)) }));\n      this.placed.push(m);\n    }\n    this.icon = hudSprite('gold-icon');\n  }\n\n  update(ctx) {\n    ctx.hud.clear();\n    ctx.hud.sprite(6, 6, this.icon.rows, this.icon.colors);\n    ctx.hud.text(26, 10, 'MARKET CORNER', { color: 'sand' });\n  }\n\n  cameraTarget() {\n    return this.target;\n  }\n\n  status() {\n    return `market: ${this.placed.length} models, ${this.lights.length} light`;\n  }\n}\n\nawait Engine.start(new MarketCorner(), withUrlOptions({ container: document.getElementById('app'), camera: { preset: 'iso', zoom: 1.6 } }));\n```\n\n## 7. Credits\n\n`CREDITS.md` says where everything the kit carries came from: the library and the built-in\nmodels are the engine's own work, three.js and Rapier ship under their licences (their texts are\nin it), and each pack's author and licence with every id it holds. Ship it with your game. A def\nyou import or copy from someone else records it in `source: { url, licence, author }`; credit it\nas its licence asks.\n","numLines":284,"startLine":1,"totalLines":284}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01LLwf8Y6jJqrREiCp4i5yRB","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
