{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SyCbfHJz2jofPcd3umQV4E","type":"tool_result","content":"1834\t### class Ragdoll\n1835\t\n1836\t- `new Ragdoll(physics: Physics, root: Object3D, parts: readonly RagdollPart[], o: RagdollOptions = {})`\n1837\t- `readonly parts: readonly RagdollPart[]`\n1838\t- `readonly o: Required<RagdollOptions>`\n1839\t- `readonly root: Object3D`\n1840\t- `get active: boolean`: Whether the bodies exist (a `physics.clear()`, a level unload, removes them: then it is off).\n1841\t- `get bodies: RAPIER.RigidBody[]`: The bodies (root part first), while active.\n1842\t- `enable(o: { velocity?: Vec3; spin?: Vec3 } = {}): void`: Make the bodies from the model's current pose, moving at `velocity` (and spinning at `spin`, rad/s).\n1843\t- `push(at: Vec3 | Vector3, velocity: Vec3): void`: Knock the part nearest `at`: it gains `velocity` (m/s, applied there as an impulse of its own mass, so the same push works whatever the ragdoll's density), and its joints pass some of it on.\n1844\t- `mass(): number`: Total mass of the parts (world units), while active.\n1845\t- `speed(): number`: Fastest part (m/s): settled when this stays low.\n1846\t- `rootPose(out = new Vector3()): { at: Vector3; faceUp: boolean; heading: number }`: Where the root part (the pelvis) is and how it lies: face up (on its back: its forward, +Z, points up) or down, and the heading (yaw) a character lying like that has: on its back its head is behind it (−Z), on its front ahead (+Z). That is the heading to get…\n1847\t- `sync(): void`: Write the bodies into the joints (between the last two physics steps). Call every frame after the physics update.\n1848\t- `release(o: { ground?: number | ((x: number, z: number) => number); heading?: number; offset?: Vec3 } = {}): { apply(w: number): void }`: Remove the bodies and hand the pose back. The model root moves under the root part (feet at `ground`: a height, or a function of x, z called once the bodies are gone; turned to `heading`, default `rootPose().heading`) without moving the joints in the world; t…\n1849\t- `disable(): void`: Remove the bodies (the joints keep the last pose).\n1850\t\n1851\t### interface RagdollOptions\n1852\t\n1853\t- `density?: number`: World density of the parts (the world's mass units per m³). Default 3.\n1854\t- `damping?: number`: Linear and angular damping (air drag, joint friction). Defaults 0.1 and 1.5.\n1855\t- `angularDamping?: number`\n1856\t- `friction?: number`: Friction of the parts on the ground. Default 0.5.\n1857\t\n1858\t### interface RagdollPart\n1859\t\n1860\t- `bone: string`: The joint (Object3D name) this part moves.\n1861\t- `parent?: string`: The part it hangs from (that part's bone); none for the root (the pelvis).\n1862\t- `from?: Vec3`: The capsule, in the joint's own space: from `from` (default the joint) to `to`.\n1863\t- `to: Vec3`\n1864\t- `radius: number`\n1865\t- `hinge?: readonly [number, number]`: How it hangs: a hinge about local X (degrees, min and max) or a ball joint with a swing cone (degrees). Default a 60° cone.\n1866\t- `cone?: number`\n1867\t- `density?: number`: Relative density (default 1).\n1868\t\n1869\t### class Rewind\n1870\t\n1871\t- `new Rewind(physics: Physics, o: RewindOptions = {})`\n1872\t- `readonly capacity: number`: Steps of history kept.\n1873\t- `rewinding: boolean`: True: each physics step goes one step back instead of recording."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4a882869-9e92-4155-a3b0-121d8fdc660c","uuid":"41289f92-9ace-4196-91d8-c59a69660ee5","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:21:45.342Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211959__x9a5b1d/work/_research/engine/x/pixel-engine/API.md","content":"### class Ragdoll\n\n- `new Ragdoll(physics: Physics, root: Object3D, parts: readonly RagdollPart[], o: RagdollOptions = {})`\n- `readonly parts: readonly RagdollPart[]`\n- `readonly o: Required<RagdollOptions>`\n- `readonly root: Object3D`\n- `get active: boolean`: Whether the bodies exist (a `physics.clear()`, a level unload, removes them: then it is off).\n- `get bodies: RAPIER.RigidBody[]`: The bodies (root part first), while active.\n- `enable(o: { velocity?: Vec3; spin?: Vec3 } = {}): void`: Make the bodies from the model's current pose, moving at `velocity` (and spinning at `spin`, rad/s).\n- `push(at: Vec3 | Vector3, velocity: Vec3): void`: Knock the part nearest `at`: it gains `velocity` (m/s, applied there as an impulse of its own mass, so the same push works whatever the ragdoll's density), and its joints pass some of it on.\n- `mass(): number`: Total mass of the parts (world units), while active.\n- `speed(): number`: Fastest part (m/s): settled when this stays low.\n- `rootPose(out = new Vector3()): { at: Vector3; faceUp: boolean; heading: number }`: Where the root part (the pelvis) is and how it lies: face up (on its back: its forward, +Z, points up) or down, and the heading (yaw) a character lying like that has: on its back its head is behind it (−Z), on its front ahead (+Z). That is the heading to get…\n- `sync(): void`: Write the bodies into the joints (between the last two physics steps). Call every frame after the physics update.\n- `release(o: { ground?: number | ((x: number, z: number) => number); heading?: number; offset?: Vec3 } = {}): { apply(w: number): void }`: Remove the bodies and hand the pose back. The model root moves under the root part (feet at `ground`: a height, or a function of x, z called once the bodies are gone; turned to `heading`, default `rootPose().heading`) without moving the joints in the world; t…\n- `disable(): void`: Remove the bodies (the joints keep the last pose).\n\n### interface RagdollOptions\n\n- `density?: number`: World density of the parts (the world's mass units per m³). Default 3.\n- `damping?: number`: Linear and angular damping (air drag, joint friction). Defaults 0.1 and 1.5.\n- `angularDamping?: number`\n- `friction?: number`: Friction of the parts on the ground. Default 0.5.\n\n### interface RagdollPart\n\n- `bone: string`: The joint (Object3D name) this part moves.\n- `parent?: string`: The part it hangs from (that part's bone); none for the root (the pelvis).\n- `from?: Vec3`: The capsule, in the joint's own space: from `from` (default the joint) to `to`.\n- `to: Vec3`\n- `radius: number`\n- `hinge?: readonly [number, number]`: How it hangs: a hinge about local X (degrees, min and max) or a ball joint with a swing cone (degrees). Default a 60° cone.\n- `cone?: number`\n- `density?: number`: Relative density (default 1).\n\n### class Rewind\n\n- `new Rewind(physics: Physics, o: RewindOptions = {})`\n- `readonly capacity: number`: Steps of history kept.\n- `rewinding: boolean`: True: each physics step goes one step back instead of recording.","numLines":40,"startLine":1834,"totalLines":5144}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01SyCbfHJz2jofPcd3umQV4E","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
