 `aura-icon` | 13 × 13 | core white, light sand, dark orange, edge plum | icon, skill, aura, buff | An aura: \n| `trap-icon` | 13 × 11 | light mist, dark slate, pan sand, edge ink | icon, skill, trap | A bear trap, open: \n| `totem-icon` | 12 × 15 | wing sky, wing2 blue, light orange, dark red, eye ink, beak sand, edge ink | icon, \n| `arrow-up` | 8 × 8 | light white, shade mist, edge ink | icon, ui, arrow, up | A white arrow pointing up: sc\n| `arrow-down` | 8 × 8 | light white, shade mist, edge ink | icon, ui, arrow, down | A white arrow pointing do\n| `arrow-left` | 8 × 8 | light white, shade mist, edge ink | icon, ui, arrow, left | A white arrow pointing le\n| `arrow-right` | 8 × 8 | light white, shade mist, edge ink | icon, ui, arrow, right | A white arrow pointing \n| `check` | 8 × 8 | body lime, shade green, edge ink | icon, ui, check, confirm | A lime check mark: yes, done\n| `cross` | 8 × 8 | body red, shade plum, edge ink | icon, ui, cross, cancel | A red X: no, close, cancel |\n| `plus` | 8 × 8 | body lime, shade green, edge ink | icon, ui, plus, add | A lime plus: add, more, a higher s\n| `minus` | 8 × 8 | body red, shade plum, edge ink | icon, ui, minus, remove | A red minus: remove, less, a lo\n| `lock` | 8 × 8 | steel mist, steel2 slate, body sand, shade orange, hole plum, edge ink | icon, ui, lock, lo\n| `gear` | 12 × 12 | light mist, dark slate, edge ink | icon, ui, gear, settings | A steel cog with eight teet\n| `magnifier` | 10 × 10 | glint white, glass cyan, glass2 sky, light mist, dark slate, handle red, edge ink | \n| `quest-marker` | 6 × 10 | glint white, light sand, shade orange, edge plum | icon, ui, quest, alert | A gold\n| `bat` | 24 × 8, 2 frames | rim slate, wing plum, body night, eye sand, edge ink | sprite, critter, bat, anim\n| `rat` | 24 × 8, 2 frames | fur mist, shade slate, pink red, eye ink, edge ink | sprite, critter, rat, animat\n| `spider` | 24 × 8, 2 frames | leg slate, body plum, sheen mist, mark red, eye sand, edge ink | sprite, critt\n| `slime` | 20 × 8, 2 frames | glint white, light lime, mid green, dark teal, eye ink, edge ink | sprite, crit\n| `butterfly` | 20 × 8, 2 frames | wing sky, wing2 blue, spot white, body night, edge ink | sprite, critter, b\n| `firefly` | 16 × 8, 2 frames | core white, glow lime, halo green | sprite, critter, firefly, light, animated\n| `fire-burst` | 48 × 12, 4 frames | core white, inner sand, flame orange, outer red, edge plum | sprite, effe\n| `ice-shards` | 36 × 12, 3 frames | core white, ice cyan, shade sky, edge navy | sprite, effect, cold, ice, a\n| `lightning-spark` | 20 × 10, 2 frames | core white, bolt sand, edge plum | sprite, effect, lightning, spark,\n| `poison-bubbles` | 24 × 8, 3 frames | glint white, light lime, mid green, edge teal | sprite, effect, poison\n| `heal-sparkles` | 24 × 10, 3 frames | core white, light lime, faded green, edge teal | sprite, effect, heal,\n| `blood-splat` | 30 × 8, 3 frames | light red, dark plum, edge ink | sprite, effect, blood, hit, animated | B\n| `dust-puff` | 30 × 8, 3 frames | light sand, mid mist, dark slate, edge night | sprite, effect, dust, animat\n\n## Packs\n### class CharacterController\n\nKinematic capsule driven by Rapier's KinematicCharacterController, with classic\nplatformer affordances (coyote time, jump buffering, variable jump height).\n\nThe body moves in continuous world space; the visual model is interpolated by\nPhysics.bind and only *looks* pixel-aligned through the render pipeline.\n\n- `new CharacterController(physics: Physics, options: CharacterOptions)`\n- `readonly body: RAPIER.RigidBody`\n- `readonly collider: RAPIER.Collider`\n- `readonly controller: RAPIER.KinematicCharacterController`\n- `readonly velocity: Vector3`\n- `grounded: boolean`\n- `facing: number`\n- `get feet: Vector3`: Feet position (bottom of the capsule), continuous world space.\n- `interpolatedFeet(alpha: number): Vector3`: Feet position blended between the previous and current physics step (render use).\n- `setInput(move: Vector3, jumpPressed: boolean, jumpHeld: boolean): void`: Set desired horizontal move direction (world space, length ≤ 1) and jump input.\n- `teleport(position: [number, number, number]): void`\n- `fixedUpdate(dt: number): void`: Call from Physics.update's fixedUpdate callback.\n- `attachAnimations(model: Object3D, clips: readonly AnimationClip[]): void`: Attach a model's animation clips (expects Idle / Walk / Jump).\n- `get animation: CharacterAnim`\n- `updateVisual(model: Object3D, dt: number): void`: Per render frame: pick animation state and advance the mixer.\n\n### interface CharacterOptions\n\n- `position: [number, number, number]`\n- `radius?: number`\n- `halfHeight?: number`: Height of the cylindrical part of the capsule.\n- `speed?: number`\n- `jumpSpeed?: number`\n- `gravity?: number`\n\n### interface Chunk\n\nBreaking a box into pieces: cut planes along each axis at jittered positions, so the\nchunks tile the box exactly (nothing missing, nothing overlapping) but look hand-broken,\nnot like a grid. Pure and seeded (the same box breaks the same way every time).\n\n  const chunks = fractureBox([2, 3, 0.4], { cuts: [3, 4, 1], jitter: 0.35, seed: 7 });\n  // [{ center: [x, y, z], size: [w, h, d] }, ...] in the box's own space\n\n- `readonly center: [number, number, number]`: Centre in the box's local space (the box is centred on the origin).\n- `readonly size: [number, number, number]`\n\n1777:### class Physics\n1778-\n1779-Rapier world with a fixed 60 Hz step and render interpolation.\n1780-\n1781-Physics owns the truth; visuals follow. Bound Object3Ds are *interpolated* between\n1782-the last two physics states for smooth motion. Pixel alignment is purely a camera /\n1783-presentation concern and never touches bodies here.\n1784-\n1785-- `static create(gravity = -24): Promise<Physics>`: Loads Rapier's wasm on first use (a separate, streamed .wasm file), then builds a world.\n1786-- `world: RAPIER.World`: The Rapier world. A new one per level (`clear()`): read it from here, don't keep it across levels.\n1787-- `alpha: number`: Interpolation factor between the previous and current physics step, 0..1.\n1788-- `steps: number`\n1789-- `readonly fields: ForceFields`: Zones that push, pull or drag (wind, fans, wells, currents): dynamic bodies get them every step, `PlatformerCharacter` reads them (physics/forces.ts).\n1790-- `stepMs: number`: Milliseconds Rapier took for one step (smoothed): what a pile of bodies costs.\n1791-- `update(dt: number, fixedUpdate?: (dt: number) => void): void`: Advance the simulation by real elapsed time. `fixedUpdate` runs before each fixed step (apply forces, move kinematic characters there).\n1792-- `state(): PhysicsState`: The physics as data, between frames (`engine.snapshot()`): the fixed step's clock and the whole Rapier world, exact. Bodies and colliders keep their handles across `setState`: a game finds its own again with `world.getRigidBody(\n1793-- `setState(s: PhysicsState): void`: Back to `state()`: the world it saved replaces this one, bound meshes re-found by handle.\n1794-- `restoreState(s: PhysicsState): PhysicsRestore`: `setState`, undoable: the saved world is built first (nothing changes if that fails), then replaces this one; `undo()` puts everything back as it was, `commit()` frees the old world. A mesh bound to a bod\n1795-- `get time: number`: Seconds of physics simulated (fixed steps × 1/60): the clock movers run on.\n1796-- `onStep(f: () => void, o: { first?: boolean } = {}): () => void`: Run `f` after every fixed step, before bound meshes (`bind`) read their bodies. Listeners run in the order they were added (instanced bodies keep their last two poses, a ragdoll holds its\n1797-- `addMover(body: KinematicBody, options: MoverOptions): Mover`: Drive a kinematic body (`RigidBodyDesc.kinematicPositionBased()`) along a path, spinning or swinging, as a pure function of its own clock (physics/movers.ts), which starts at 0 now: the same\n1798-- `conveyor(collider: RAPIER.Collider, velocity: readonly [number, number, number] | null): void`: Make a collider a conveyor belt moving at `velocity` (m/s, world axes): dynamic bodies touching it are dragged along, the character standing on it is carrie\n1799-- `beltVelocity(handle: number): readonly [number, number, number] | null`: A conveyor's velocity, by collider handle (null: not a belt).\n1800-- `explode(at: readonly [number, number, number] | Vector3, o: ExplosionOptions = {}): number`: Push every dynamic body near `at` away from it (physics/forces.ts). Returns how many.\n1801-- `bind(body: RAPIER.RigidBody, object: Object3D): void`: Make `object` follow `body` (interpolated).\n1802-- `unbind(object: Object3D): void`\n1803-- `addStaticBox(o: BoxOptions): RAPIER.Collider`\n1804-- `addStaticCylinder(position: [number, number, number], halfHeight: number, radius: number): RAPIER.Collider`\n1805-- `addDynamicBox(o: BoxOptions): RAPIER.RigidBody`\n1806-- `tag(collider: RAPIER.Collider, ...tags: string[]): RAPIER.Collider`: Tag a collider with gameplay semantics the character controller understands: 'climbable' (ladders/vines), 'pushable', 'grabbable', 'slippery', 'noLedge', 'character', 'noCamera' (came\n1807-- `hasTag(collider: RAPIER.Collider | null | undefined, tag: string): boolean`","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NgL6ts37dYFBUfkZbEdJQ8","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
