es into Run (default: their authored\n     * speeds). Gaits with different stance shares don't blend cleanly (one foot is still\n     * planted while the other gait already swings it), so keep the band short.\n     */\n    blend?: readonly [number, number];\n}\nexport interface AnimatorOptions {\n    rig?: RigSpec;\n    probe?: GroundProbe;\n    feet?: Partial<FootPlacementTuning>;\n    layers?: Partial<PoseLayerTuning>;\n    gait?: GaitClips;\n}\n/** Everything the procedural passes need this frame. */\nexport interface ProceduralInput extends PoseLayerInput {\n    feet: FootPlacementInput;\n}\nexport declare class Animator {\n    readonly model: Object3D;\n    private readonly mixer;\n    private readonly rotationBlend;\n    private readonly layers;\n    private readonly byName;\n    private current;\n    /** Gait: actions in role order (tiptoe, walk, run), stride per cycle (m), stance shares, phase 0..1. */\n    private readonly gait;\n    readonly feet: FootPlacement | null;\n    readonly pose: PoseLayers | null;\n    private readonly footNames;\n    /**\n     * The animated pose of every joint the procedural passes change, saved after the mixer and\n     * put back before the next mixer update. three's mixer only writes a joint whose blended\n     * value changed, so a held pose would otherwise keep (and stack) last frame's offsets.\n     */\n    private readonly touched;\n    constructor(model: Object3D, clips: readonly AnimationClip[], rest: ReadonlyMap<string, Quaternion>, options?: AnimatorOptions);\n    dispose(): void;\n    duration(name: string): number | undefined;\n    authoredSpeed(name: string): number | undefined;\n    /** The clip a request shows most (the gait's dominant clip). */\n    dominant(req: AnimRequest): string;\n    /** Tooling: every clip contributing to the pose, with its share of the blend, time (s) and rate. */\n    mix(): {\n        name: string;\n        weight: number;\n        time: number;\n        rate: number;\n    }[];\n    /** Start over with `name` playing alone, no blends, no procedural memory (a teleport, a respawn). */\n    restart(name: string): void;\n    /** Switch to (or keep playing) what `req` asks for, fading over `fade` seconds. */\n    play(req: AnimRequest, fade: number): void;\n    /** Advance fades, the gait and the mixer, then the procedural passes. */\n    update(dt: number, procedural?: ProceduralInput): void;\n    /** Gait shares and phase: weights from the speed, rates matched to each clip's own speed. */\n    private stepGait;\n    /**\n     * Which foot the gait swings and where it will land (foot placement blends a swinging\n     * foot from the ground it left to the ground it lands on); null when no gait leads.\n     */\n    private swingOf;\n    private readonly swing;\n    private readonly swingR;\n    private readonly swingL;\n    private gaitShares;\n    /** Normalised phase of a layer, if it is a stride (a gait clip with an authored speed). */\n    private phaseOf;\n    private isStride;\n    /**\n     * Starting the gait from another clip (standing, landing): the foot that is further forward\n     * now is the planted one, at the point of its stance where the gait has it that far\n     * forward (mid-stance from standing, heel strike landing with a leg out front), and the\n     * other one takes the next step.\n     */\n    private startPhase;\n    private stop;\n}\n262:    attachModel(model: Object3D, clips: readonly AnimationClip[], rig?: RigSpec): void;\n### skyAt()\n\n```ts\nfunction skyAt(hour: number): SkyState\n```\n\nThe sky at `hour` (wraps around 24).\n\n### interface SkyState\n\n- `readonly sunDir: [number, number, number]`: Unit vector toward the sun (or the moon, at night).\n- `readonly sunColor: number`\n- `readonly sunIntensity: number`\n### applySky()\n\n```ts\nfunction applySky(engine: Pick<Engine, 'sun' | 'ambient' | 'scene' | 'setSunDirection'>, s: SkyState): void\n```\n\nPut a sky on the engine: sun direction, colour and strength, ambient light, background.\n\n### bayer4()\n\n```ts\nfunction bayer4(): any\n```\n\nA 4 x 4 ordered dither threshold per art pixel (0..1): keep a pixel where it is below its opacity.\n\n460:### class Settings\n461-\n462-`engine.settings`: the player's settings, applied to the engine and saved. A field the page URL\n463-sets (`?look=`, `?mode=`, `?res=`, `?quality=`, `?fps=`, `?debug=`: review flags) wins over a\n464-saved one at start (which stays saved). `open`, `close` and `toggle` show and hide the\n465-settings panel.\n466-\n467-- `new Settings(host: SettingsHost, key: string | null)`\n468-- `readonly key: string | null`\n469-- `get values: Readonly<PlayerSettings>`: The player's choices in effect: fields left out are the game's (or a review flag's).\n470-- `get isOpen: boolean`\n471-- `set(patch: PlayerSettings): void`: Change some settings: applied at once and saved. A field set to `undefined` goes back to the game's.\n472-- `reset(): void`: Forget every choice, the held ones too: the game's own picture again.\n--\n492:### class SettingsPanel\n493-\n494-The settings panel (DOM, like the debug panel: it stays legible at any art resolution) and the\n495-⚙ button that opens it: the player's picture, sound and engine options (`engine.settings`,\n496-settings.ts; the AudioManager's volumes). The engine pauses the game while it is open. Keys\n497-pressed in it never reach the game; Escape or Done closes it.\n498-\n499-- `new SettingsPanel(engine: Engine, container: HTMLElement, corner: TouchCorner | false)`\n500-- `readonly root: HTMLDivElement`\n501-- `readonly button: HTMLButtonElement | null`\n502-- `show(): void`: Show the panel with the engine's current values. The panel takes the focus, not a control: a game key pressed out of habit (D, Space) must not pick an option; Tab reaches the controls.\n503-- `hide(): void`\n504-- `sync(): void`: Put the engine's current values into the controls, and into the debug panel (the loop fills it only while the game runs).\n358:### interface PlayerSettings\n359-\n360-The player's settings: the standard picture and engine options every game gets, as plain data\n361-(sound is the AudioManager's, which keeps its own volumes). A field left out is the game's own\n362-choice; a field set is the player's and wins over it. `engine.settings` holds them, applies\n363-them, saves them per game and shows them in the settings panel (the ⚙ button).\n364-\n365-- `look?: string`: A LOOK_PRESETS name. Left out: the look the game gives each level.\n366-- `pixelArt?: boolean`: Pixel art (the pixel pass), or false for smooth 3D (render mode `raw`).\n367-- `pixelSize?: 'fine' | 'chunky'`: The art resolution: `fine` (the game's, 480×270 by default) or `chunky` (two thirds of it: bigger pixels).\n368-- `quality?: QualityOption`: Shadow and light quality: a level, or `auto` (the device's).\n369-- `fps?: number`: Frame cap: 60, 30, or 0 for the display's own rate.\n370-- `debugInfo?: boolean`: The debug panel: frame rate, camera, GPU errors and the game's status.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_011yWbrTw4QCHps3gvAgA6xN","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
