{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011TtrNDs9bi8mM56mFPuq8Y","type":"tool_result","content":"### skyAt()\n\n```ts\nfunction skyAt(hour: number): SkyState\n```\n\nThe sky at `hour` (wraps around 24).\n\n### interface SkyState\n\n- `readonly sunDir: [number, number, number]`: Unit vector toward the sun (or the moon, at night).\n- `readonly sunColor: number`\n- `readonly sunIntensity: number`\n- `readonly ambientColor: number`\n- `readonly ambientIntensity: number`\n- `readonly sky: number`: Background (sky) and fog colour.\n- `readonly night: number`: 0 by day, 1 deep at night: lanterns, stars, windows.\n\n### interface Snapshot\n\n- `readonly format: 1`\n- `readonly engine: string`: The engine version that took it (a different one may not restore the same).\n- `readonly game: string`: The game's name: a snapshot restores into the same game.\n- `readonly seed: number`: The engine seed and game time when it was taken.\n- `readonly time: number`\n- `readonly clock: ClockState`\n- `readonly random: number`: `ctx.random`'s state.\n- `readonly physics: PhysicsState`\n5073:### interface WaterOptions\n5074-\n5075-- `size: readonly [number, number]`: Width (x) and depth (z) of the surface, m.\n5076-- `at: readonly [number, number, number]`: Centre of the surface at rest.\n5077-- `segments?: readonly [number, number]`: Grid quads along x and z (default: one per ripple cell, or 4 per metre without ripples).\n5078-- `waves?: readonly Wave[]`\n5079-- `ripples?: RippleField | null`: A ripple field covering the same rectangle (its size and centre must match).\n5080-- `deep?: number`: Colours (hex): troughs, crests, foam.\n5081-- `shallow?: number`\n5082-- `foam?: number`\n5083-- `foamAt?: number`: Height above rest (m) where foam starts. Default: 75% of the waves' combined height (the tallest crests).\n5084-- `opacity?: number`: 1: opaque; less: see-through by a 4×4 ordered dither per art pixel.\n5085-\n5086-### class WaterSurface\n5087-\n4580:### class Precipitation\n4581-\n4582-- `new Precipitation(o: PrecipitationOptions)`\n4583-- `readonly kind: PrecipitationKind`\n4584-- `readonly area: readonly [number, number, number]`\n4585-- `readonly wind: Vector2`: Wind (m/s along x and z): rain slants, snow drifts.\n4586-- `get intensity: number`: Share of the drops falling (0..1).\n4587-- `get speed: number`: Fall speed (m/s).\n4588-- `update(dt: number, center: Vector3): void`: Per frame (game time): advance the fall and follow `center`.\n4589-- `splashes(dt: number): number`: How many drops hit the ground in `dt` seconds at this intensity (for splash particles, ripples).\n4590-- `dispose(): this`: Frees the GPU-related resources allocated by this instance\n4598:### interface PrecipitationOptions\n4599-\n4600-- `kind: PrecipitationKind`\n4601-- `count: number`: Most drops at once (the instance count).\n4602-- `area?: readonly [number, number, number]`: Width, height and depth of the air the drops fall through, around the centre.\n4603-- `color?: number`: Drop colour (hex).\n4604-- `speed?: number`: Fall speed (m/s). Rain 16, snow 1.4.\n4605-\n4606-### interface Recording\n4607-\n4608-- `readonly format: 1`\n4049:### interface CameraKey\n4050-\n4051-- `at: number`: Time (s) the camera is exactly here.\n4052-- `position: V3`\n4053-- `target: V3`: The point it looks at.\n4054-- `fov?: number`: Vertical field of view (degrees); default the previous key's, or 50.\n4055-- `cut?: boolean`: Jump here instead of gliding from the key before (a cut to a new shot).\n4056-\n4057-### class CameraShake\n4058-\n4059-- `trauma: number`\n4060-- `maxOffset: number`: World units at full trauma.\n4061-- `decay: number`: Trauma lost per second.\n4062-- `strength: number`: Global multiplier (settings: 0 turns shake off).\n4063-- `readonly offset: Vector3`\n--\n4071:### interface CameraShot\n4072-\n4073-- `position: [number, number, number]`\n4074-- `target: [number, number, number]`\n4075-- `fov: number`\n4076-\n4077-### interface ClockState\n4078-\n4079-A clock as data.\n4080-\n4081-- `readonly scale: number`\n4082-- `readonly hitstop: number`\n4083-\n4084-### coversPixel()\n4085-\n2982:### hudSprite()\n2983-\n2984-```ts\n2985-function hudSprite(idOrDef: string | TextureDef, o: TextureOptions & { frame?: number } = {}): { rows: string[]; colors: Record<string, PaletteColor | number> }\n2986-```\n2987-\n2988-One frame as `hud.sprite` rows and colours: a character per slot (a, b, c, … in palette order),\n2989-'.' for transparent.\n2990-\n2006:### interface TriggerOptions\n2007-\n2008-- `onEnter?(other: RAPIER.Collider, trigger: Trigger): void`: Called once when a collider starts overlapping the volume.\n2009-- `onExit?(other: RAPIER.Collider, trigger: Trigger): void`: Called once when it stops overlapping (or leaves the world).\n2010-- `tag?: string`: Only colliders carrying this tag (e.g. 'character', which PlatformerCharacter sets).\n2011-- `filter?(other: RAPIER.Collider): boolean`: Extra filter: return false to ignore a collider.\n2012-- `includeStatic?: boolean`: Also report colliders on fixed bodies (level geometry). Default false.\n2013-- `once?: boolean`: Remove the trigger after its first enter (pickups).\n2014-- `rotationY?: number`: Rotation about Y in radians.\n2015-\n2016-### type TriggerShape\n2017-\n2018-```ts\n1402-- `broken: boolean`\n1403-\n1404:### interface BreakableOptions\n1405-\n1406-- `at: Vec3`: Centre and full size of the block.\n1407-- `size: Vec3`\n1408-- `rotationY?: number`: Turn about Y (radians).\n1409-- `color: PaletteColor`\n1410-- `cuts?: Vec3`: Pieces along x, y, z (default [3, 3, 1]).\n1411-- `jitter?: number`\n1412-- `seed?: number`\n1413-- `linger?: number`: Seconds the pieces lie around before they dissolve (default 4).\n1414-- `density?: number`: Chunk density (default 1.5).\n1415-- `tags?: string[]`\n1416-\n1417-### class Breakables\n1418-\n1419-- `new Breakables(ctx: Ctx)`\n1420-- `readonly blocks: Breakable[]`\n1421-- `readonly tiles: Crumble[]`\n14