{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjC6ezvSXJotyb4Ct8Hh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The map text checks out and the script fits the font, but two tests showed the engine's conveyor lacks a CharacterController, so belts need their own code. I'm fixing that, the speed note that contradicted its code, and adding the missing in-game HUD section.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6481,"cache_read_input_tokens":486266,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6481},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4a882869-9e92-4155-a3b0-121d8fdc660c","uuid":"54d7aec7-72c9-4efa-a8c8-cb525e93547d","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:01:05.575Z","request_id":"req_011CgjC6egaCiRNncUx3L2w9","narration_block_indexes":[0],"thinking_duration_ms":1,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjC6ezvSXJotyb4Ct8Hh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PpsSf8dUR5cscXDwjtbSP5","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"W=/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211959__x9a5b1d/work; cd $W && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'; t=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\ndef rep(a,b,n=1):\n    global t\n    assert t.count(a)>=1, 'missing: '+a[:70]\n    t=t.replace(a,b) if n==0 else t.replace(a,b,n)\n\n# speed: the note and the code must agree\nrep(\"- **Body:** `new CharacterController(physics, { position, speed: 1, radius: 0.3, halfHeight: 0.5 })`, tag its collider `noCamera`. Each fixed step call `setInput(moveVector, false, false)` and `fixedUpdate(dt)`. **[verified]** Speed is `options.speed` × the move vector's length, so build the controller with the top speed and scale the vector. Worlds are flat (ground at y=0), so there are no stairs: ladders and floors are scripted.\",\n    \"- **Body:** `new CharacterController(physics, { position, speed: TUNING.runSpeed, radius: 0.3, halfHeight: 0.5 })`, tag its collider `noCamera` and `player`. Each fixed step call `setInput(moveVector, false, false)` and `fixedUpdate(dt)`. **[verified]** Velocity is `speed` × the move vector's length (half a vector at speed 4 moves at 2 m/s) and walls stop it, so build the controller with the top speed and scale the vector. Worlds are flat (ground at y=0), so there are no stairs: ladders and floors are scripted.\")\n# shots must not pass through props\nrep(\"then `ctx.physics.castRay(o, d, 80, ['noCamera', 'character'])` for the world, then ray tests against hit zones. Nearest wins.\",\n    \"then `ctx.physics.castRay(o, d, 80, ['player', 'enemy'])` for the world (so bullets still hit props tagged `noCamera`), then ray tests against hit zones. Nearest wins.\")\nrep(\"- `ctx.physics.castRay(from, dir, max, ignoreTags, excludeBody)`.\\n\",\n    \"- `ctx.physics.castRay(from, dir, max, ignoreTags, excludeBody)`. Tags are free strings (`physics.tag(collider, 'player')`).\\n- `physics.conveyor` doesn't carry a `CharacterController`. Add the belt's velocity yourself from the map cell under the feet.\\n\")\n# nav and water\nrep(\"`NavGrid.fromRows(rows, { cell: 1, origin: [-W/2, 0, -H/2], blocked: '#T~H…' })` (keep `#T~HBS` closed, others open; toggle doors and gates with `setOpen`).\",\n    \"`NavGrid.fromRows(rows, { cell: 1, origin: [-W/2, 0, -H/2], blocked: '#T~HBSG' })`. Open `B`, `S` and `G` cells with `setOpen` when they break or open. `D`, `W`, `E` and `L` stay open in nav and are solid only for Max until used (§4.8).\")\nrep(\"| `~` | Deep water, blocked; player and enemies die/drown if knocked in | `S` | Roll-up shutter |\",\n    \"| `~` | Deep water. An invisible wall stops Max. Enemies kicked in sink and die | `S` | Roll-up shutter |\")\nrep(\"| `=` | Planks | `c` | Conveyor belt, walkable, carries you (`physics.conveyor`) |\",\n    \"| `=` | Planks | `c` | Conveyor belt, walkable, carries whoever stands on it (add velocity by map cell) |\")\nrep(\"Two belts running opposite ways (`physics.conveyor`), carcasses\",\"Two belts running opposite ways, 1.5 m/s, carcasses\")\nrep(\"kick enemies off the edge (`~` kills them, Max's kick has no fall risk).\",\"kick enemies off the edge (`~` kills them).\")\n# printed map note\nrep(\"The quay, printed, for orientation (north up; the pier is bottom right, the Net Loft top centre, the chapel left, the sea right, the Foghorn rock top right):\",\n    \"The quay, printed for orientation, with repeated rows left out (north up; the pier is bottom right, the Net Loft top centre, the chapel left, the sea right, the Foghorn rock top right):\")\n# dawn was not rendered\nrep(\"**Moods [verified: they look right]:**\",\"**Moods (dusk, rain and abbey [verified: they look right]; dawn is a first guess, so check it):**\")\n# hub boot as valid code\nrep(\"\"\"if (window.AIHub?.active) {\n  const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\n  if (info) return startSession(info); // straight to the card: no title, menu, attract or storage reads\n}\nstartStandalone();\n\"\"\",\"\"\"async function boot() {\n  if (window.AIHub?.active) {\n    const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\n    if (info) return startSession(info); // straight to the card: no title, menu or attract\n  }\n  return startStandalone();\n}\n\"\"\")\nrep(\"The README is short; read it. The examples `examples/arena.html` (shared world) show a working pattern.\",\n    \"The README is short; read it. `examples/arena.html` in the same folder is a complete shared-world game, including the server case.\")\n# dev page\nrep(\"pixel-engine.js check.mjs packs/ package.json\\n\",\"pixel-engine.js check.mjs packs/ package.json\\nindex.html               dev page that loads src/main.js as a module (what the kit's check.mjs plays)\\n\")\n# rig patch is not an engine edit\nrep(\"- **Camera:** yaw and pitch are game state, shared by explore and aim so nothing snaps. Patch the engine's third-person rig on its instance **[verified]**:\",\n    \"- **Camera:** yaw and pitch are game state, shared by explore and aim so nothing snaps. The engine's `third` rig orbits but has no shoulder offset, so replace `step` on the rig instance at runtime (the engine file stays untouched) **[verified]**:\")\n# attract exception\nrep(\"Runs on touch-only devices too, where tapping doesn't exit.\",\"Runs on touch-only devices too, where tapping doesn't exit. It never starts while a Night Shift lobby is open or in a hub session.\")\n# intent timing\nrep(\"This one rule makes attract mode, the playthrough test and co-op easy.\",\n    \"This one rule makes attract mode, the playthrough test and co-op easy. `HumanIntent` reads held buttons with `isDown` and presses with `consumePress` in `fixedUpdate` (the engine runs `fixedUpdate` before `update`, zero or more times per frame), and look from `input.mouseDelta` in `update`.\")\n# sharing clips, and her back\nrep(\"Each `buildModel` returns its own object.\",\"Each `buildModel` returns its own object. Compile each clip set once and share the `AnimationClip`s between instances of the same proportions: each instance only needs its own mixer.\")\nrep(\"Giants: `object.scale.setScalar(2.6)`\",\"The camera sits behind Max all game, so her back is her best side: hair covering the back of the head, scarf, coat belt and seam.\\n\\nGiants: `object.scale.setScalar(2.6)`\")\n# in-game HUD\nrep(\"### Screens (all in `src/screens/`)\\n\",\"\"\"### In-game HUD (`src/game/hud.js`)\nSparse, and gone during cutscenes. Bottom left: `COVERAGE` (Max's health bar; flashes `LAPSED` under 25%) with the Dame's bar under it when she's with you. Bottom right: ammo at scale 2 (`12/15`), weapon icon, grenade count. Top right: Doubloons, only for 3 s after they change. Top left: objective line. Bottom centre: the one context prompt, glyph and verb. Centre: the laser dot (no crosshair). Low health adds a heartbeat and a pulsing `red` screen edge. Damage direction: a short red arc at the screen edge. Drawn with `hud.clear()` then redraw every frame.\n\n### Screens (all in `src/screens/`)\n\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(t)\nprint('ok', t.count('\\n'), len(t.encode()))\nEOF\ngrep -n 'speed: 1,\\|physics.conveyor\\|\\[.noCamera., .character.\\]' PLAN.md | cut -c1-160","description":"Apply corrections and additions to the plan"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6481,"cache_read_input_tokens":486266,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6481},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_