{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjCC3o1rqoGzVpFU1MPX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VfWN4tGgV2RNAN9FYNjY91","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"W=/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211959__x9a5b1d/work; cd $W && grep -n -i -E 'bicorne|tiny|very small|scale 0\\.7|short|hat still|the hat|knife man|knife-fighting|Ansgar|duel|closing shutter|I AM NOT' PLAN.md | cut -c1-210","description":"Find every mention of the villain's size and the duel"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":17193,"cache_read_input_tokens":500095,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":17193},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4a882869-9e92-4155-a3b0-121d8fdc660c","uuid":"57cfa0ce-7f56-4009-bcd7-d74611b0106a","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:02:09.851Z","request_id":"req_011CgjCC3WA7aNHmWayN5JCE","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01VfWN4tGgV2RNAN9FYNjY91":{"command":"W=/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211959__x9a5b1d/work; cd $W && grep -n -i -E 'bicorne|tiny|very small|scale 0\\.7|short|hat still|the hat|knife man|knife-fighting|Ansgar|duel|closing shutter|I AM NOT' PLAN.md | cut -c1-210","description":"Find every mention of the villain's size and the duel"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VfWN4tGgV2RNAN9FYNjY91","type":"tool_result","content":"47:**Originality guardrails. None of these may appear:** Leon, Ashley, Ada, Luis, Krauser, Salazar, Saddler, Hunnigan; Las Plagas, Los Ganados, Umbrella, Raccoon City; Spain or Spanish-speaking villagers; the s\n57:| **Max Ransom** | Maxine Ransom, field adjuster, Ostrander Mutual Assurance. Dry, tired, unkillable. Sunglasses at night (\"They're prescription\"). | Grey trench coat (long skirt), short sand-coloured hair, \n58:| **Dame Ottoline Vane** | 74, tiny, imperious. Keeps a ledger of deductions from your fee. Not helpless: she operates machinery and fights with a cane in her solo segment. | Fur coat, ebony cane, handbag, h\n59:| **Commodore Anselm Thole** | Self-styled lord of the island. Very small, very loud, enormous bicorne hat. Talks over the Tannoys. Hates having his sentences interrupted. | Scale 0.7, giant hat, medals |\n64:| **Mate Ansgar** | First mate, knife man. One QTE duel. | Pea coat, gaff scar |\n70:- Max never raises her voice. Her jokes are one short sentence, usually a policy term.\n105:Buy: Sold, and no refunds from the deep. / A fine choice for a short life.\n148:(Hatch torn open. He is very small in there.)\n149:COMMODORE: I AM NOT SHORT. THE ISLAND IS TALL.\n327:`src/game/qte.js`: a large glyph (device-correct) in a shrinking ring at screen centre, `engine.timeScale = 0.5` while open. Types: press (window 0.9 s; dev slider), mash (fill a bar), alternate (Cross/Circ\n474:6. **Duel:** Mate Ansgar steps out in the north corridor. Interactive cutscene, 4 press QTEs and 1 mash (§4.11), ending with Max throwing him under the closing shutter. Telegraph in the corridor before it (\n507:A walking brass ball on legs (`HERO_RIG` root scale 2.4; brass ball torso, porthole with the tiny Commodore inside, pipes, steam `smoke` particles). Water rises by phase.\n509:- **Phase 2, Hatch.** All valves gone: he sags. Three hatch locks (60 HP each). Shoot them while he flails; then a Kick prompt (cutscene: Max climbs, tears the hatch).\n510:- **Phase 3, The Mother.** Out he falls, and the thing on his neck bursts out and takes the altar: a 3.5 m limpet with the Commodore fused on top, hat still on. It spits brine globs (shootable, 20) and birt\n523:- Mode **`shared-world`**, seats `[1, 4]`, own card. Follow https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md. Vendor `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` from \n613:- **Characters:** Max, the Dame, Islander (×3 palettes, sou'wester, cap, bare), Net-Wife, Bottler, Deckhand, Carrier (sack), Flenser, Re-Salted, Monk, Reliquary Knight, Drowned, Harpooner, Mate Ansgar, Nils\n640:- **Others:** SawRev, SawSwing, SawLunge; ShieldWalk, ShieldBlock, FlailSpin; KnightWalk (heavy gait), HalberdSweep; DrownedRise; CarrierShoulder, CarrierWalk; DameWalk (tiny steps, cane), DameCane, DameBar\n668:| `dawn` | Short resolve for the launch ending |\n677:| Max | Triangle, mid (170 Hz), short, level |\n702:Sparse, and gone during cutscenes. Bottom left: `COVERAGE` (Max's health bar; flashes `LAPSED` under 25%) with the Dame's bar under it when she's with you. Bottom right: ammo at scale 2 (`12/15`), weapon ic\n842:7. **Chapter 2:** road, cannery, Dame, Flenser, winch, duel, Bosun.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4a882869-9e92-4155-a3b0-121d8fdc660c","uuid":"10978e70-ba01-469b-aa3c-b432bbd4d752","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:02:09.870Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"47:**Originality guardrails. None of these may appear:** Leon, Ashley, Ada, Luis, Krauser, Salazar, Saddler, Hunnigan; Las Plagas, Los Ganados, Umbrella, Raccoon City; Spain or Spanish-speaking villagers; the s\n57:| **Max Ransom** | Maxine Ransom, field adjuster, Ostrander Mutual Assurance. Dry, tired, unkillable. Sunglasses at night (\"They're prescription\"). | Grey trench coat (long skirt), short sand-coloured hair, \n58:| **Dame Ottoline Vane** | 74, tiny, imperious. Keeps a ledger of deductions from your fee. Not helpless: she operates machinery and fights with a cane in her solo segment. | Fur coat, ebony cane, handbag, h\n59:| **Commodore Anselm Thole** | Self-styled lord of the island. Very small, very loud, enormous bicorne hat. Talks over the Tannoys. Hates having his sentences interrupted. | Scale 0.7, giant hat, medals |\n64:| **Mate Ansgar** | First mate, knife man. One QTE duel. | Pea coat, gaff scar |\n70:- Max never raises her voice. Her jokes are one short sentence, usually a policy term.\n105:Buy: Sold, and no refunds from the deep. / A fine choice for a short life.\n148:(Hatch torn open. He is very small in there.)\n149:COMMODORE: I AM NOT SHORT. THE ISLAND IS TALL.\n327:`src/game/qte.js`: a large glyph (device-correct) in a shrinking ring at screen centre, `engine.timeScale = 0.5` while open. Types: press (window 0.9 s; dev slider), mash (fill a bar), alternate (Cross/Circ\n474:6. **Duel:** Mate Ansgar steps out in the north corridor. Interactive cutscene, 4 press QTEs and 1 mash (§4.11), ending with Max throwing him under the closing shutter. Telegraph in the corridor before it (\n507:A walking brass ball on legs (`HERO_RIG` root scale 2.4; brass ball torso, porthole with the tiny Commodore inside, pipes, steam `smoke` particles). Water rises by phase.\n509:- **Phase 2, Hatch.** All valves gone: he sags. Three hatch locks (60 HP each). Shoot them while he flails; then a Kick prompt (cutscene: Max climbs, tears the hatch).\n510:- **Phase 3, The Mother.** Out he falls, and the thing on his neck bursts out and takes the altar: a 3.5 m limpet with the Commodore fused on top, hat still on. It spits brine globs (shootable, 20) and birt\n523:- Mode **`shared-world`**, seats `[1, 4]`, own card. Follow https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md. Vendor `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` from \n613:- **Characters:** Max, the Dame, Islander (×3 palettes, sou'wester, cap, bare), Net-Wife, Bottler, Deckhand, Carrier (sack), Flenser, Re-Salted, Monk, Reliquary Knight, Drowned, Harpooner, Mate Ansgar, Nils\n640:- **Others:** SawRev, SawSwing, SawLunge; ShieldWalk, ShieldBlock, FlailSpin; KnightWalk (heavy gait), HalberdSweep; DrownedRise; CarrierShoulder, CarrierWalk; DameWalk (tiny steps, cane), DameCane, DameBar\n668:| `dawn` | Short resolve for the launch ending |\n677:| Max | Triangle, mid (170 Hz), short, level |\n702:Sparse, and gone during cutscenes. Bottom left: `COVERAGE` (Max's health bar; flashes `LAPSED` under 25%) with the Dame's bar under it when she's with you. Bottom right: ammo at scale 2 (`12/15`), weapon ic\n842:7. **Chapter 2:** road, cannery, Dame, Flenser, winch, duel, Bosun.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01VfWN4tGgV2RNAN9FYNjY91","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjCEceGRfvwwjYPoi2zM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MxuWMyLFNmKtQmFHG4c2i3","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"W=/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211959__x9a5b1d/work; cd $W && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'; t=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global t\n    assert t.count(a)==1, ('count %d: '%t.count(a))+a[:70]\n    t=t.replace(a,b)\nrep(\"| **Commodore Anselm Thole** | Self-styled lord of the island. Very small, very loud, enormous bicorne hat. Talks over the Tannoys. Hates having his sentences interrupted. | Scale 0.7, giant hat, medals |\",\n    \"| **Commodore Anselm Thole** | Self-styled lord of the island, and its radio announcer. For the whole game he is only a huge, rich voice on the Tannoys, and he hates being interrupted. Never seen until the final boss: a gaunt old man in slippers, at a microphone, in an armchair inside his machine. | Scale 1.2, thin, peaked cap, far too many medals, dressing gown under the coat |\")\nrep(\"| **Mate Ansgar** | First mate, knife man. One QTE duel. | Pea coat, gaff scar |\",\n    \"| **Mate Ansgar** | First mate, cannery bruiser with a gaff hook. One fight on the conveyor belt. | Pea coat, broad, hook |\")\nrep(\"(Hatch torn open. He is very small in there.)\\nCOMMODORE: I AM NOT SHORT. THE ISLAND IS TALL.\\n\",\n    \"(Hatch torn open. An old man in slippers, in an armchair, at a microphone.)\\nCOMMODORE: THIS IS AN OUTRAGE. I AM ON THE AIR.\\nMAX: Not for long.\\n\")\nrep(\"(Final settlement. She stamps the form on his forehead.)\\nMAX: Claim denied.\\n\",\n    \"(Final settlement. The microphone is gone. His jaw keeps moving. The voice keeps coming, from the thing on his neck. It always did.)\\n(She stamps the form on it.)\\nMAX: Claim denied.\\n\")\nrep(\"| Big set-piece siege that ends abruptly |\",\"| Big set-piece siege that ends abruptly |\")\nrep(\"6. **Duel:** Mate Ansgar steps out in the north corridor. Interactive cutscene, 4 press QTEs and 1 mash (§4.11), ending with Max throwing him under the closing shutter. Telegraph in the corridor before it (autosave).\",\n    \"6. **The belt:** crossing the hall to the shutter, Max is hooked off her feet by Mate Ansgar's gaff, and they go down together on the belt, riding toward the can press at its east end. Interactive cutscene, 4 press QTEs and 1 mash (§4.11). He goes into the press. A can rolls out. Telegraph in the north corridor (autosave).\")\nrep(\"porthole with the tiny Commodore inside, pipes,\",\"porthole showing an armchair and a figure at a microphone, pipes,\")\nrep(\"a 3.5 m limpet with the Commodore fused on top, hat still on. It spits brine globs (shootable, 20) and births Limpets; flares kill them all at once. The hat has 200 HP; then his head has 400. Then **Final Settlement:** QTE (press, press, mash); stamp; `Claim denied.`\",\n    \"a 3.5 m limpet with the Commodore fused on top, still broadcasting. It spits brine globs (shootable, 20) and births Limpets; flares kill them all at once. The brass microphone on his chest has 200 HP: shooting it cuts him off mid-sentence one last time, and this is the horror beat, because the voice carries on without it. Then the eye under his jaw has 400 HP. Then **Final Settlement:** QTE (press, press, mash); stamp; `Claim denied.`\")\n# the source-mapping table and the writing rule should agree with the new villain\nrep(\"| Radio support, villain taunts | Mr. Pym on the Claims Desk (with on-hold music); the Commodore over island loudspeakers |\",\n    \"| Radio support, villain taunts | Mr. Pym on the Claims Desk (with on-hold music); the Commodore, an unseen voice on island loudspeakers |\")\nrep(\"- The Commodore speaks in full theatrical sentences, in capitals, and always over a loudspeaker.\",\n    \"- The Commodore speaks in full theatrical sentences, in capitals, always over a loudspeaker, like a man reading the shipping forecast to the condemned.\")\nrep(\"**Mate Ansgar** | First mate\",\"**Mate Ansgar** | First mate\") if False else None\n# clips for the belt fight\nrep(\"BosunDrag, BosunSweep,\",\"AnsgarHook, AnsgarSwing; BosunDrag, BosunSweep,\")\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(t)\nprint('ok')\nEOF\ngrep -n 'Mate Ansgar\\|duel' PLAN.md | cut -c1-170; grep -n 'Used in: Flenser dodge' PLAN.md | cut -c1-220","description":"Redesign the villain and the duel to stay clearly original"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4500,"cache_read_input_tokens":517288,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4500},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4a882869-9e92-4155-a3b0-121d8fdc660c","uuid":"ef9e1253-4ebf-42ad-8e3c-9019edbc7ab1","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:02:25.929Z","request_id":"req_011CgjCEcMQ7BVhj23shb5ov","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01MxuWMyLFNmKtQmFHG4c2i3":{"command":"W=/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211959__x9a5b1d/work; cd $W && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'; t=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global t\n    assert t.count(a)==1, ('count %d: '%t.count(a))+a[:70]\n    t=t.replace(a,b)\nrep(\"| **Commodore Anselm Thole** | Self-styled lord of the island. Very small, very loud, enormous bicorne hat. Talks over the Tannoys. Hates having his sentences interrupted. | Scale 0.7, giant hat, medals |\",\n    \"| **Commodore Anselm Thole** | Self-styled lord of the island, and its radio announcer. For the whole game he is only a huge, rich voice on the Tannoys, and he hates being interrupted. Never seen until the final boss: a gaunt old man in slippers, at a microphone, in an armchair inside his machine. | Scale 1.2, thin, peaked cap, far too many medals, dressing gown under the coat |\")\nrep(\"| **Mate Ansgar** | First mate, knife man. One QTE duel. | Pea coat, gaff scar |\",\n    \"| **Mate Ansgar** | First mate, cannery bruiser with a gaff hook. One fight on the conveyor belt. | Pea coat, broad, hook |\")\nrep(\"(Hatch torn open. He is very small in there.)\\nCOMMODORE: I AM NOT SHORT. THE ISLAND IS TALL.\\n\",\n    \"(Hatch torn open. An old man in slippers, in an armchair, at a microphone.)\\nCOMMODORE: THIS IS AN OUTRAGE. I AM ON THE AIR.\\nMAX: Not for long.\\n\")\nrep(\"(Final settlement. She stamps the form on his forehead.)\\nMAX: Claim denied.\\n\",\n    \"(Final settlement. The microphone is gone. His jaw keeps moving. The voice keeps coming, from the thing on his neck. It always did.)\\n(She stamps the form on it.)\\nMAX: Claim denied.\\n\")\nrep(\"| Big set-piece siege that ends abruptly |\",\"| Big set-piece siege that ends abruptly |\")\nrep(\"6. **Duel:** Mate Ansgar steps out in the north corridor. Interactive cutscene, 4 press QTEs and 1 mash (§4.11), ending with Max throwing him under the closing shutter. Telegraph in the corridor before it (autosave).\",\n    \"6. **The belt:** crossing the hall to the shutter, Max is hooked off her feet by Mate Ansgar's gaff, and they go down together on the belt, riding toward the can press at its east end. Interactive cutscene, 4 press QTEs and 1 mash (§4.11). He goes into the press. A can rolls out. Telegraph in the north corridor (autosave).\")\nrep(\"porthole with the tiny Commodore inside, pipes,\",\"porthole showing an armchair and a figure at a microphone, pipes,\")\nrep(\"a 3.5 m limpet with the Commodore fused on top, hat still on. It spits brine globs (shootable, 20) and births Limpets; flares kill them all at once. The hat has 200 HP; then his head has 400. Then **Final Settlement:** QTE (press, press, mash); stamp; `Claim denied.`\",\n    \"a 3.5 m limpet with the Commodore fused on top, still broadcasting. It spits brine globs (shootable, 20) and births Limpets; flares kill them all at once. The brass microphone on his chest has 200 HP: shooting it cuts him off mid-sentence one last time, and this is the horror beat, because the voice carries on without it. Then the eye under his jaw has 400 HP. Then **Final Settlement:** QTE (press, press, mash); stamp; `Claim denied.`\")\n# the source-mapping table and the writing rule should agree with the new villain\nrep(\"| Radio support, villain taunts | Mr. Pym on the Claims Desk (with on-hold music); the Commodore over island loudspeakers |\",\n    \"| Radio support, villain taunts | Mr. Pym on the Claims Desk (with on-hold music); the Commodore, an unseen voice on island loudspeakers |\")\nrep(\"- The Commodore speaks in full theatrical sentences, in capitals, and always over a loudspeaker.\",\n    \"- The Commodore speaks in full theatrical sentences, in capitals, always over a loudspeaker, like a man reading the shipping forecast to the condemned.\")\nrep(\"**Mate Ansgar** | First mate\",\"**Mate Ansgar** | First mate\") if False else None\n# clips for the belt fight\nrep(\"BosunDrag, BosunSweep,\",\"AnsgarHook, AnsgarSwing; BosunDrag, BosunSweep,\")\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(t)\nprint('ok')\nEOF\ngrep -n 'Mate Ansgar\\|duel' PLAN.md | cut -c1-170; grep -n 'Used in: Flenser dodge' PLAN.md | cut -c1-220","description":"Redesign the villain and the duel to stay clearly original"}}}
